"locale":"en"},"8665":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-77","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"`start_background`","locale":"en"},"8666":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-78","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"8667":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-79","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"`False` (default, as the command line)","locale":"en"},"8668":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-80","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"A call with `wait=True` runs the job on the calling thread and returns it finished. Ctrl+C while it runs cancels it (the job comes back with `state == \"cancelled\"`). A job submitted without `wait` **does not run**: there is no scheduler","locale":"en"},"8669":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-81","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"`True` (as the server)","locale":"en"},"8670":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-82","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"Starts the scheduler and the unloading of idle models. A call without `wait` queues the job and returns at once; jobs queue for the GPU and other resources. Wait for one with `s.jobs.wait(job.id, timeout)`","locale":"en"},"8671":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-83","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#events","content":"`events.subscribe(handler)` registers a callback and returns a function that unsubscribes it. The callback runs on the thread that raised the event, so return quickly. The event types are the socket's (see HTTP API), defined in `mizuoto.core.events.models`:","locale":"en"},"8672":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-84","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#errors","content":"Failures raise subclasses of `mizuoto.core.errors.MizuotoError`, one for each error the API returns:","locale":"en"},"8673":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-85","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#errors","content":"A failure **while the job runs** raises nothing: `speak(..., wait=True)` returns a job with `state == \"failed\"` and the cause in `job.error` (`code`, `message`, `detail`). What raises is what can be found before running (an unknown model, invalid parameters, a licence not accepted…). The error codes are listed in HTTP API.","locale":"en"},"8674":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-86","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#embedding-the-server","content":"`MizuotoServer` starts, inside your program, the server `mizuoto webui` runs: the same API, web UI and jobs. The host program chooses where the data and the settings go, which settings cannot be changed, and the path the UI sits under.","locale":"en"},"8675":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-87","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#embedding-the-server","content":"`import mizuoto` does not load FastAPI; the server part loads when `MizuotoServer` is used. `from mizuoto.embed import MizuotoServer, serve` works too.","locale":"en"},"8676":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-88","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#arguments","content":"Argument","locale":"en"},"8677":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-89","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#arguments","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"8678":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-90","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"typ