anced-embed-139","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"The web UI's address, the port, whether it serves","locale":"en"},"8728":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-140","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"`services`","locale":"en"},"8729":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-141","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"The services the server uses (see above), callable once started","locale":"en"},"8730":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-142","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"The object is also a context manager:","locale":"en"},"8731":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-143","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"`serve(block=False, **options)` creates a server with the same arguments, starts it and returns it; with `block=True` it serves in the foreground.","locale":"en"},"8732":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-144","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#pinned-settings","content":"The values in `settings` sit above the settings file and the environment, are **never written to the file**, and cannot be changed through the web UI or the API:","locale":"en"},"8733":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-145","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#pinned-settings","content":"In the web UI's **Settings**, a pinned value is marked **Set by the application Mizuoto runs in** (one set by an environment variable: **Set by an environment variable**). `settings.view().pinned` lists the pinned names.","locale":"en"},"8734":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-146","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"With `api_prefix=\"/voice\"` the web UI is at `<address>/voice/`, the API at `/voice/api/v1/...` and the OpenAI-compatible API at `/voice/v1/...`. The web UI derives the prefix from its own script's URL; nothing else to configure.","locale":"en"},"8735":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-147","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"By default only local names are accepted in `Host` (against DNS rebinding). Behind a tunnel or a reverse proxy, add the public name with `extra_hosts=[\"abc.example.com\"]` or `server.allow_host(\"https://abc.example.com\")`. Requests through such names are never treated as local, so the server-machine-only features (browsing server files and so on) are closed to them.","locale":"en"},"8736":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-148","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"Once it is reachable, anyone with the address can use it: set `access_token`, or add authentication of your own. HTTP API details the access checks.","locale":"en"},"8737":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-149","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"Once started, the server writes `server.json` (`host`, `port`, `url`, `pid`) into the data folder so other programs can find it; `stop()` removes it.","locale":"en"},"8738":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-150","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#mounting-into-an-existing-fastapi-app","content":"When the host program is itself a FastAPI (or other ASGI) application, it can mount Mizuoto instead of opening another port:","locale":"en"},"8739":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-e