ocale":"en"},"10176":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"10177":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"`$XDG_DATA_HOME/mizuoto`, else `~/.local/share/mizuoto`","locale":"en"},"10178":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-28","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"10179":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-29","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"`~/Library/Application Support/mizuoto`","locale":"en"},"10180":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-30","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"10181":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-31","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"`%APPDATA%\\mizuoto`","locale":"en"},"10182":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-32","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"`MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR` or `mizuoto webui --data-dir <path>` puts it elsewhere. `settings.toml` sits in the data folder unless `MIZUOTO_CONFIG_DIR` or `webui --config-dir` names another folder for it (the data stays in the data folder). **Settings** › **About** in the web UI shows the **Data folder** and the **Settings file**.","locale":"en"},"10183":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-33","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#the-data-folder-and-the-settings-file","content":"To have `mizuoto config`, `mizuoto speak` and the rest use the same data folder as a server, the environment variable is the easy way: `--data-dir` is an option of `webui` only.","locale":"en"},"10184":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-34","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#layout","content":"The `paths.*` settings move models, voices, outputs, datasets, experiments, projects and caches elsewhere one by one; empty means inside the data folder, and so does a relative folder (`results` is `<data folder>/results`, whatever folder Mizuoto is started from).","locale":"en"},"10185":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-35","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#viewing-and-changing-settings","content":"Keys are dotted; values are parsed as JSON (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), else taken as a string; `null` clears a setting that may be empty. The whole file is validated before it is written: a value out of range, of the wrong type, or an unknown key is an error (exit code 4) and the file stays as it was.","locale":"en"},"10186":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-36","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#viewing-and-changing-settings","content":"Dictionary settings take new keys: `engines.<engine id>.<field>`, `engines.<engine id>.load_options.<option>`, `tts.model_aliases.<alias>`. `mizuoto config set` does not check load option names and values; the web UI and the API check them against the engine's manifest.","locale":"en"},"10187":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-37","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#viewing-and-changing-settings","content":"`config show` and `config get` never show tokens, only whether `access_token_configured` and `token_configured` are set; `config set` on a token prints `(hidden)`. `config show` also lists `resolved_paths` (the folders in use where settings are empty), `env_overrides` (the environment variables in effect) and `pinned` (what the embedding application pins).","locale":"en"},"10188":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#viewing-and-changing-settings","content":"A running server reads changes to the file within about a second, and open web UIs refresh; saving in the web UI afterwards merges with the file as it is, so it keeps the command line's changes. A broken file makes the server log `Ignored a change to … settings.toml` and keep its settings. `server.host`, `server.port` and the certificates take effect the next time the server starts; changing `engines.<id>.*` unloads that engine's models, which load with the new settings when next used.","locale":"en"},"10189":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#viewing-and-changing-settings","content":"Keys Mizuoto does not know are ignored when `settings.toml` is read.","locale":"en"},"10190":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"`mizuoto env vars` lists the environment variables Mizuoto reads, and the `MIZUOTO_*` variables set now:","locale":"en"},"10191":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"10192":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"10193":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"`MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR`","locale":"en"},"10194":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-44","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"The data folder","locale":"en