remote add`, which also checks that the host answers.","locale":"en"},"10586":{"id":"/en/docs/cli","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Command line"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli","locale":"en"},"10587":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"The mizuoto command line calls the same core as the web UI and the HTTP API: this page covers its shared conventions, foreground jobs, exit codes, and using it while a server runs.","locale":"en"},"10588":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#the-commands","content":"The commands","locale":"en"},"10589":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"How it differs from the web UI","locale":"en"},"10590":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Output and `--json`","locale":"en"},"10591":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Exit codes","locale":"en"},"10592":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-5","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#debugging-and-logs","content":"Debugging and logs","locale":"en"},"10593":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-6","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"Using it while a server runs","locale":"en"},"10594":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-7","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#common-workflows","content":"Common workflows","locale":"en"},"10595":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-8","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#check-the-engines-download-a-model-speak","content":"Check the engines, download a model, speak","locale":"en"},"10596":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-9","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#clone-and-design-voices","content":"Clone and design voices","locale":"en"},"10597":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-10","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#hear-it-as-it-is-made","content":"Hear it as it is made","locale":"en"},"10598":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-11","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#batches-and-parameters","content":"Batches and parameters","locale":"en"},"10599":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-12","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#transcribe-convert-and-edit","content":"Transcribe, convert and edit","locale":"en"},"10600":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-13","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#training","content":"Training","locale":"en"},"10601":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-14","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#projects","content":"Projects","locale":"en"},"10602":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-15","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-completion","content":"Shell completion","locale":"en"},"10603":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-16","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"Next","locale":"en"},"10604":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-17","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"The `mizuoto` command line does what the web UI does: speak, clone and design voices, convert and edit recordings, transcribe, check torch and the engines, manage models, presets, projects, datasets and training, remote hosts, jobs and settings. It is a thin wrapper: each command parses its arguments, calls the **one** core method for that operation and prints the result. The HTTP API behind the web UI calls the same methods, so both behave alike, and the records `--json` prints have the same shape as the API's JSON.","locale":"en"},"10605":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-18","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"This page covers the shared conventions and common workflows; every command's options are in the Command reference, settings and environment variables in Configuration and environment variables.","locale":"en"},"10606":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-19","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#the-commands","content":"Add `--help` at any level; a group name alone (such as `mizuoto model`) shows that group's help too. Every level accepts `--debug`.","locale":"en"},"10607":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-20","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**Jobs run in the foreground.** `speak`, `design`, `model download`, `train run`, `project render` and the like create a job and run it in the terminal until it ends; a progress bar goes to stderr (only when stderr is a terminal, and not with `--json`), with bytes, speed and time left for downloads.","locale":"en"},"10608":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-21","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**Ctrl+C cancels the job.** The job is marked **Cancelled**, the engine stops at its next check (the next token or step), a training stage's process is stopped, and the command exits with code 130.","locale":"en"},"10609":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-22","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**No server needed.** Each command opens the data folder (settings, database, models) itself and closes it when done; the engines run in the command's own process and the models it loaded go with it, so every `speak` loads its model again. For many sentences in a row, a server (the web UI or the HTTP API) is faster: it keeps models loaded.","locale":"en"},"10610":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-23","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**Any path works.** The web UI reads server files only inside **Folders the browser may open** (`paths.browse_roots`); `--ref`, `model import`, `dataset import` and the like take any path on this machine.","locale":"en"},"10611":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-24","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"List and info commands print tables; with `--json` they print JSON in the shape of the matching API record, for scripts:","locale":"en"},"10612":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-25","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"A few details:","locale":"en"},"10613":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"`speak` prints each result's path, duration and sample rate. Results are always kept in the outputs folder (and appear in **History**); `-o` also copies one to the path you give, whose extension picks the format.","locale":"en"},"10614":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"`speak --json` prints `{\"job\": …, \"outputs\": […]}`: the finished job and the output records it made.","locale":"en"},"10615":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-28","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"`speak --plan` checks the request and prints the plan (model, device, voice mode, segments, parameters) without running anything.","locale":"en"},"10616":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-29","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Warnings (such as dropped parameters the model does not take) go to stderr, starting with `warning:`, never into stdout.","locale":"en"},"10617":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-30","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A failing command prints the error and, when the error names a fix, the command to run on the next line; the exit code tells the kind of error. The codes are defined in `mizuoto/core/codes.py`, each error class's exit code in `mizuoto/core/errors.py`:","locale":"en"},"10618":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-31","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Exit code","locale":"en"},"10619":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-32","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Error code","locale":"en"},"10620":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-33","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Typical cause","locale":"en"},"10621":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-34","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"0","locale":"en"},"10622":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-35","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Success","locale":"en"},"10623":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-36","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"1","locale":"en"},"10624":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-37","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`internal_error`","locale":"en"},"10625":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An unclassified internal error; answering \"no\" to a confirmation","locale":"en"},"10626":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"2","locale":"en"},"10627":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`not_found`","locale":"en"},"10628":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Unknown model, voice, job, output or engine. Click also exits with 2 for command-line mistakes (unknown option, value out of range)","locale":"en"},"10629":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"3","locale":"en"},"10630":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`conflict`, `busy`","locale":"en"},"10631":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-44","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A name exists already; a stage is running; `webui` finds no free port","locale":"en"},"10632":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-45","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"4","locale":"en"},"10633":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-46","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`invalid_input`, `invalid_path`, `capability_not_supported`, `parameter_not_supported`, `parameter_out_of_range`, `reference_invalid`, `language_not_supported`","locale":"en"},"10634":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-47","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An invalid request: the model lacks that voice mode or parameter, a reference clip is too short or too long, an unsupported language; `webui`'s certificate file is missing","locale":"en"},"10635":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-48","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"5","locale":"en"},"10636":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-49","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`licence_not_accepted`","locale":"en"},"10637":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-50","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A licence-gated engine (Fish Speech, IndexTTS) whose licence is not accepted yet","locale":"en"},"10638":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-51","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"7","locale":"en"},"10639":{"id":"/en/docs/cl