 GB (`MIZUOTO_TEST_SETTINGS='{\"compute\": {\"vram_limit_mb\": 4096}}'`, less than the large models (Fish Speech S2 Pro, IndexTTS 2, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B) need, so they stream and load partly through the whole stack; 2 h 6 min). The slowest capped test is a long Qwen3-TTS request (the narrator fine-tune's seed test: 2,778 s alone against 322 s whole): an autoregressive model that streams copies its streamed layers once per token.","locale":"en"},"12819":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-759","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"2026-10-19, one RTX 3090 (`cuda:0`) on a quiet machine, the G0 cases streamed (`perf/g8/` in the experiment workspace: `run.sh`, `single.sh`, `monitor.py`, which samples the card's used memory and the process tree's RAM every 0.2 s; 0.1's engine workers are counted with its host). Warm request and time to first audio are the best of runs 2–3; `stack.py` records `first_chunk_seconds`.","locale":"en"},"12820":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-760","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"Case","locale":"en"},"12821":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-761","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"Warm, 0.1 → native","locale":"en"},"12822":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-762","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"First audio, 0.1 → native","locale":"en"},"12823":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-763","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"