tent":"3,116 / 3,301 / 9,094","locale":"en"},"12908":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-848","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"2,970 / 3,301 / 9,094","locale":"en"},"12909":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-849","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"The old rule of thumb was under nearly all of them (GPT-SoVITS 5×, VoxCPM's `lowest` LoRA up to 3.4×), and said 14.1 GB for Fish Speech's LoRA, which runs out of a 24 GB card at its default batch. Estimates are now these peaks scaled by the base model's size, plus a tenth and 512 MB, and follow the batch where the peak does; the warning names a batch that fits when no preset does.","locale":"en"},"12910":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-850","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"Measured on the RTX 3090s (2026-10-18) with torch 2.8.0+cu128, flash-attn 2.8.3 (the only wheel for torch 2.8), xFormers 0.0.32.post2 (in an environment of its own: it does not import beside flash-attn 2.8.3) and SageAttention 1.0.6 (Triton; 2.x needs `nvcc`, SageAttention 3 a Blackwell GPU). Every site's calls were recorded from the G0 set's requests (17 sites, 36 kinds of call) and each backend that takes a call was run on it against what `auto` computes.","locale":"en"},"12911":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-851","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"**Kernels.** FlashAttention and xFormers agree with `auto` to bf16/fp16 rounding everywhere (cosine 1.000000); SageAttention quantises: cosine 0.98 on BERT, 0.78 (max error 12) on VoxCPM's bidirectional DiT attention. At these sizes the packages are slower than SDPA per call (single-query steps 0.13–0.5×, prompts 0.15–0.9×), except where FlashAttention skips padded keys: VoxCPM's steps over its preallocated cache, 4.4× (head dim 128) and 2.3× (64).","locale":"en"},"12912":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-852","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"**Requests**, warm time against `auto` and the audio against `auto`'s (the G0 set, one GPU, quiet, three runs a case; \"other take\": a different realisation of the request, as another seed would give):","locale":"en"},"12913":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-853","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"Case","locale":"en"},"12914":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-854","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"`sdpa`","locale":"en"},"12915":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-855","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"`flash`","locale":"en"},"12916":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-856","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"`xformers`","locale":"en"},"12917":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-857","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","content":"`sage` (before `approx_ok`)","locale":"en"},"12918":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-858","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#attention-backends-on-a-gpu","