e#partly-loaded-models","content":"4,775","locale":"en"},"13006":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-946","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"0.554 s, 9.03 GB/s","locale":"en"},"13007":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-947","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"0.485 s, 10.33 GB/s","locale":"en"},"13008":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-948","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"The copies themselves now run at 13.2 GB/s (98 % of the link, measured over the talker's own host tensors); what remains of a reload is allocating the device memory again, 0.08–0.1 s for the talker, since giving memory up empties the allocator's cache (on purpose: other processes get it back). Expandable segments allocate no faster. The smaller models have more small tensors, which stay pageable (under 1 MB). Under a cap, the streamer used to copy streamed weights into page-locked memory at 1.5 GB/s on the first request; registering them in place took that off the cold request: F5-TTS 5.40 → 4.99 s, OmniVoice 5.96 → 5.07 s, CosyVoice 2/3 20.82/16.93 → 19.36/14.10 s, GPT-SoVITS v4 6.51 → 5.65 s, Fish Speech 44.89 → 41.23 s, IndexTTS 2 36.10 → 33.54 s, VoxCPM 2 29.12 → 26.85 s, Qwen3-TTS 9.22/10.90 → 8.57/9.86 s; warm requests and every output identical.","locale":"en"},"13009":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-949","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"**Streaming** under a cap left Qwen3-TTS bound by kernel launches, not copies: the GPU was busy 7.5 of 12.9 s, since a streamed talker decoded without its CUDA graphs. Graphs now run over a streamed `sequence` handle whose layers rest in page-locked memory, each step's graphs copying its streamed weights in (see Memory):","locale":"en"},"13010":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-950","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"Case (cap)","locale":"en"},"13011":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-951","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"Eager while streaming","locale":"en"},"13012":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-952","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"Graphs while streaming","locale":"en"},"13013":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-953","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"Audio","locale":"en"},"13014":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-954","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"Qwen3-TTS 1.7B custom voice (4 GB)","locale":"en"},"13015":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-955","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"6.62 s","locale":"en"},"13016":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-956","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"**5.00 s** (1.32×)","locale":"en"},"13017":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-957","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#partly-loaded-models","content":"identical","locale":"en"},"13018":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-958