-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-modes-and-a-real-out-of-memory","content":"**A real out-of-memory**, not the test's injected one: under an 8 or 12 GB cap with the allocator capped as well, a thread took the remaining memory while a request was generating, down to 64 KB fragments. Qwen3-TTS's talker and IndexTTS 2's GPT (at two moments) ran out in the allocator itself, ran again with half their weights streamed (`oom_retries`, the warning, `meta.memory.partial`: \"capped at half its weights after running out of memory\"), and gave the undisturbed run's audio sample for sample. Taken a moment later, after the talker had finished, the same squeeze made the codec decoder's placement see 218 MB free and the talker give up memory instead: no error, the same audio. (`compute.vram_limit_mb` alone tells the runtime, not the allocator: the squeeze then took the whole GPU, which is why the allocator was capped for this.)","locale":"en"},"13091":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1031","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#torchcompile-on-the-cpu","content":"`compute.compile`, fp32, 8 threads; time of the compiled module, warm:","locale":"en"},"13092":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1032","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#torchcompile-on-the-cpu","content":"Engine","locale":"en"},"13093":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1033","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#torchcompile-on-the-cpu","content":"Module","locale":"en"},"13094":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1034","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#torchcompile-on-the-cpu","content":"Change","locale":"en"},"13095":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1035","