"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"CPU fp32","locale":"en"},"13624":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-113","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Max abs error ≤ 1e-5 × max(1, ‖ref‖∞); cosine ≥ 0.99999","locale":"en"},"13625":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-114","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"GPU bf16/fp16","locale":"en"},"13626":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-115","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Cosine ≥ 0.999","locale":"en"},"13627":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-116","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**T2 Stage**","locale":"en"},"13628":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-117","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Teacher-forced logits; discrete outputs from captured inputs (speech-tokenizer codes, VQ codes, ODE trajectories with injected noise)","locale":"en"},"13629":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-118","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"CPU fp32","locale":"en"},"13630":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-119","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Argmax agreement 100 %; discrete agreement ≥ 99.9 % with every flip inspected and explained (e.g. ties at FSQ rounding boundaries); trajectories within T1","locale":"en"},"13631":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-120","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**T3 End to end, seeded**","locale":"en"},"13632":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-121","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"A full request through Mizuoto's stack: native against reference, same seed, same torch","locale":"en"},"13633":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-122","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"CPU fp32","locale":"en"},"13634":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-123","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**Identical tokens; audio identical or max abs error ≤ 1e-4**; exceptions listed per engine with a reason","locale":"en"},"13635":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-124","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**T4 Statistical**","locale":"en"},"13636":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-125","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Corpus runs in each engine's production dtype and device, native against reference; seeds not aligned (GPU kernels differ)","locale":"en"},"13637":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-126","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"GPU (bf16/fp16), CPU","locale":"en"},"13638":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-127","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Over ≥ 20 texts × 3 voices × 3 seeds per voice per voice mode and model: mean CER/WER (Whisper large-v3-turbo) ≤ reference + 0.5 pp, and no case worse than the reference's worst + 5 pp; speaker similarity (CAM++ cosine to the reference clip) mean ≥ reference − 0.01; duration ratio within ±5 %; UTMOS mean ≥ reference − 0.05; loudness and F0 median within the reference's interquartile range, per voice. Failed clips (error rate above 50 %) are compared on their own (Fisher's exact test) and left out of the other measures; a threshold exceeded fails only when the paired difference is significant (Wilcoxon, p \\< 0.05)","locale":"en"},"13639":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-128","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**Why T3 is judged on the CPU in fp32 only.** Any logit difference flips a multinomial draw (or a beam) and everything after it diverges. On GPUs in reduced precision even upstream does not match itself bit for bit (batched against single greedy decoding, for one), so GPU consistency is judged by T1's per-module error plus T4's statistics.","locale":"en"},"13640":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-129","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**Behaviour beyond the audio** is part of the comparison too, checked through the contract suite on both implementations: applied parameters and warnings, the voice-mode resolution (`fit`), streaming granularity and chunk counts, cancel behaviour, error codes for invalid inputs (a reference too long, an unsupported language, a missing transcript), output sample rates, segment joins.","locale":"en"},"13641":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-130","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"Acceleration and speed work keep to the same tiers: an acceleration that changes bits (compilation, for one) stays at least within the engine's T1/T3 tolerance, with the measured error recorded; speed work on the default path must not change a bit.","locale":"en"},"13642":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-131","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#tiers-and-tolerances-of-behavioural-consistency","content":"**T0's DSP fixtures are identical on the machine class that made them**: x86-64 Linux with AVX2 and without AVX-512, under the same torch. Elsewhere the kernels round differently (numpy's AVX-512 `exp` and `log`, the Windows CRT's libm, torch's FFT and soxr's SIMD on Arm, another torch), so `tests/runtime/test_dsp.py` checks there that the outputs agree within that rounding: max abs error ≤ 1e-4 × max(1, ‖ref‖∞) in float32, 1e-12 × max(1, ‖ref‖∞) in float64. CI's macOS, Windows and AVX-512 runners measured up to 4e-5.","locale":"en"},"13643":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-132","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"`scripts/parity/quality.py` runs the tier (commands in `scripts/parity/README.md`). The corpus (`scripts/parity/corpus/t4.json`) is 17 sets, each a model and a voice mode: three voices (for cloning the corpus's two English clips and one Chinese clip; three preset speakers; three designed voices) read 20 texts (10 English, 10 Chinese, no digits) with seeds 1–3, 180 clips a set and side. Native runs in this checkout; the reference is 0.1 for every engine it had and upstream's package for VoxCPM, each in its own production dtype on its own RTX 3090. The judges: Whisper large-v3-turbo through Mizuoto's ASR (English by words, Chinese by characters, traditional characters mapped to simplified with OpenCC's table), CAM++ (CosyVoice's), UTMOS22 strong (SpeechMOS), BS.1770 loudness and YIN F0.","locale":"en"},"13644":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-133","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Three refinements came from the first full run, and the tier's rule above includes them:","locale":"en"},"13645":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-134","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"**Failures are counted, not averaged.** A runaway (a sampled model that does not stop, or keeps generating silence) has an unbounded error rate: one clip at 965 % moved Qwen3-TTS's mean from 1.3 % to 6.7 %. Clips above 50 % are counted per side and compared with Fisher's exact test; the other measures use the clips that did not fail.","locale":"en"},"13646":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-135","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"**A threshold exceeded needs a significant difference.** With 180 sampled clips, the worst clip and a 0.05 UTMOS margin move by chance: a set fails only where the paired test (by voice and text, seeds averaged) gives p \\< 0.05.","locale":"en"},"13647":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-136","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"**Targeted reruns decide single outliers.** The two runaways the corpus found, Qwen3-TTS's English speaker reading Chinese and IndexTTS 1.5 falling silent mid-sentence, were rerun with 10 seeds for that voice and language on both sides: the reference fails as often (3 and 3 of 100; 2 and 3 of 100). Both are upstream's behaviour.","locale":"en"},"13648":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-137","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Measured 2026-10-18 (reference → native; failed clips reference / native):","locale":"en"},"13649":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-138","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Set","locale":"en"},"13650":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-139","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Error rate %","locale":"en"},"13651":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-140","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Failed","locale":"en"},"13652":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-141","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Speaker similarity","locale":"en"},"13653":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-142","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Duration ratio","locale":"en"},"13654":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-143","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"UTMOS","locale":"en"},"13655":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-144","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Verdict","locale":"en"},"13656":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-145","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"Qwen3-TTS 1.7B Base, cloning","locale":"en"},"13657":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-146","page_id":"/en/