-testing-310","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"F5-TTS / GPT-SoVITS v4 / IndexTTS 1.5 / VoxCPM 2","locale":"en"},"13822":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-311","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"1.45 → 1.52 / 1.52 → 1.88 / 0.55 → 0.68 / 0.91 → 0.88","locale":"en"},"13823":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-312","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"0 / 0 (IndexTTS 1 / 1)","locale":"en"},"13824":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-313","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"within 0.004","locale":"en"},"13825":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-314","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"within 0.03","locale":"en"},"13826":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-315","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"pass (GPT-SoVITS's worst clip within noise)","locale":"en"},"13827":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-316","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"`compute.attention=fast` without flash-attn installed is SDPA everywhere, so its audio is identical. With it, F5-TTS has no padded half-precision call for FlashAttention. GPT-SoVITS v4's DiT gives one row of key lengths for its guided batch of two, which flash-attn refused (`seqlens_k must have shape (batch_size)`) until the backend expanded the lengths to the query's batch; it now takes those 704 calls.","locale":"en"},"13828":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-317","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#t4-results","content":"The first opt-in runs exposed a harness bug: requests and the parity cases had put engine options under `options`, which the request model does not have and pydantic ignores, so `packed_guidance` and six T3 cases (GPT-SoVITS's cut5, batch and serial cases, VoxCPM's continuation and retry) had run with the defaults. They now use `engine_options`; rerun on the CPU, the six are identical to 0.1 and upstream sample for sample with their options applied.","locale":"en"},"13829":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-318","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`mizuoto/webui/src/**/*.test.ts` run with vitest; `python scripts/dev.py test-web` runs `bun run test` and then `bun run typecheck` (vue-tsc). Besides unit tests of components and stores, a few rule tests guard the whole UI: `imports.test.ts`, `tokens.test.ts`, `layout.test.ts`, `ui/layers.test.ts` and `i18n/i18n.test.ts` (the same keys in both languages); see Web UI.","locale":"en"},"13830":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-319","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`python scripts/dev.py typegen-check` regenerates `schema.d.ts` and compares it with the committed one; it fails when the API changed and the types were not regenerated.","locale":"en"},"13831":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-320","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"The docs site (`site/`) has its own vitest tests; `src/lib/i18n-content.test.ts` requires a `<slug>.en.mdx` for every Chinese `<slug>.mdx` and the same page order in both sidebars.","locale":"en"},"13832":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-321","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs on every push to a branch and every pull request, with torch's CPU build (`https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu`). Mizuoto and the two gated packages are released on their own, so each is checked on its own, and a change runs only the checks for what it changes. Packages are installed with uv (`astral-sh/setup-uv`, `UV_SYSTEM_PYTHON=1`: into the Python that `setup-python` provides, no virtual environment; the cache stays off, since unpacked torch wheels would crowd the 10 GB cache limit).","locale":"en"},"13833":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-322","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"The first job, `scope`, reads the changed files (a push's from the compare API, a pull request's from its file list) and `python scripts/ci.py scope` maps them to checks:","locale":"en"},"13834":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-323","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Changed","locale":"en"},"13835":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-324","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Checks","locale":"en"},"13836":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-325","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`packages/native/<id>/**`","locale":"en"},"13837":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-326","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"that package's `gated` and `oldest-mizuoto` jobs, and `torch` for it","locale":"en"},"13838":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-327","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`mizuoto/webui/**`","locale":"en"},"13839":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-328","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`web`","locale":"en"},"13840":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-329","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`site/**`","locale":"en"},"13841":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-330","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`site` (the docs site's tests and build)","locale":"en"},"13842":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-331","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"anything else under `mizuoto/`, `tests/`, `scripts/`, `pyproject.toml`, or a new path","locale":"en"},"13843":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-332","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`host`, `web` (its API types come from the code), `torch`, and both packages' jobs: they run on Mizuoto's runtime at this commit","locale":"en"},"13844":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-333","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`.github/workflows/**`, `scripts/ci.py`","locale":"en"},"13845":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-334","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"everything","locale":"en"},"13846":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-335","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`README*.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `LICENSE`, `Dockerfile`, `.gitignore`…","locale":"en"},"13847":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-336","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"nothing","locale":"en"},"13848":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-337","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"A new branch, a manual run, a list the compare API cuts short (300 files) or a failure to read it checks everything; `tests/test_ci.py` covers the mapping.","locale":"en"},"13849":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-338","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Job","locale":"en"},"13850":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-339","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Environment","locale":"en"},"13851":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-340","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Steps","locale":"en"},"13852":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-341","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`host`","locale":"en"},"13853":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-342","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Ubuntu, Windows, macOS × Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13","locale":"en"},"13854":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-343","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`uv pip install torch` from the CPU index, then `-e . pytest pytest-cov ruff ty httpx tomli` (Mizuoto alone); in every cell `dev.py lint` (the whole repository), `dev.py typecheck-py --python-version <cell> --python-platform <cell> mizuoto tests scripts` (the standard library's stubs differ between Pythons and platforms) and `python -m pytest -q tests`; each of the three runs even when another failed","locale":"en"},"13855":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-344","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`gated`","locale":"en"},"13856":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-345","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"each package in scope × Ubuntu, Windows, macOS × Python 3.10, 3.13","locale":"en"},"13857":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-346","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`-e . -e packages/native/<id>`; `ruff check`, `ruff format --check` and `typecheck-py` of `packages/native/<id>` (sources and tests), `pytest` of its `tests/`","locale":"en"},"13858":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-347","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`oldest-mizuoto`","locale":"en"},"13859":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-348","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"each package in scope, Ubuntu, Python 3.12","locale":"en"},"13860":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-349","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"The package on the oldest Mizuoto its `pyproject.toml` allows (`python scripts/ci.py lower-bound <id>`), from PyPI: its tests run outside the checkout, with only `tests/` on `PYTHONPATH`, so `import mizuoto` finds the released one (the range check, which compares the range with Mizuoto at this commit, is left out)","locale":"en"},"13861":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-350","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"`torch`","locale":"en"},"13862":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-351","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#ci","content":"Ubuntu, Python 3.12, torch 2.8.0 and the latest release","locale":"en"},"13863