py`, ComfyUI's `ModelPatcher` without the diffusion parts) wraps one `nn.Module` with weights: its `name` (shown in the loaded-models list, e.g. `omnivoice/omnivoice:model`), `load_device`, `offload_device` (the CPU), `kind` (`sequence` for an autoregressive LM, else `oneshot`) and its sizes (`size_bytes`, `loaded_bytes`, `streamed_bytes`, `host_bytes`). The engine only reads `module`; a `LoadedEngine` lists its handles in `self.handles`."],[15121,"A `Name:` prefix counts as a speaker only when one of these holds; otherwise the whole line, prefix included, is the narrator's:"],[10759,"A `Site` names one computation and holds its **reference**: exactly what upstream computed there, with the same arguments. Mizuoto declares 19, the dummy engine's included."],[13999,"A `Trainer` subclass with a `stage_<id>(ctx)` per stage, its heavy imports inside the methods. Draw from the process-wide generators in upstream's order, or from private generators where upstream reseeded; report with `ctx.progress`, `ctx.metric` and `ctx.log`. Packages training needs beyond inference go in `REQUIRES`."],[9351,"A backend that cannot take a call falls back to the next one, ending with the model's own computation. Reasons include: not installed, the wrong GPU, a mask it does not support, a head size, fp32, a backward pass it lacks, or a kernel error. Each reason is logged once. Running out of memory is not a fallback: the memory retry handles it. With `compute.attention_strict` the request fails instead."],[11693,"A batch draws its random numbers differently; voices and parameters are per call"],[8299,"A binary message is always audio; everything else is JSON text. The whole audio is still stored as a result (`output_id`). The client may send `{\"type\": \"cancel\"}` at any time."],[11715,"A binary message is always audio; when the model falls behind the player waits instead of dropping speech"],[15119,"A blank line"],[9449,"A CA bundle, or the agent's own certificate when it is self-signed"],[10563,"A CA bundle, or the agent's own certificate when it is self-signed; empty: the system's CAs"],[9400,"A cache of the files hosts sent: `<cache>/remote/files/<sha256>/`"],[8668,"A call with `wait=True` runs the job on the calling thread and returns it finished. Ctrl+C while it runs cancels it (the job comes back with `state == \"cancelled\"`). A job submitted without `wait` **does not run**: there is no scheduler"],[15762,"A cast of voices reads a book, a script or a dialogue line by line"],[15813,"A cast of voices reads a book, a script or a dialogue line by line, each speaker with its own model and voice; changed lines are rendered again, and a chapter or the whole project is exported as one file with subtitles."],[10787,"A change applies to models loaded afterwards; a change to `engines.<id>.attention` unloads that engine."],[13506,"A change to an engine's code takes effect in a new process: restart the server, or run the command again."],[13423,"A change to any `engines.<id>.*` setting unloads that engine's models (`unload_engine`), so the next request loads them with the new device, dtype or load options."],[15389,"A clip"],[15437,"A clip longer than the model allows follows **Settings › Speech › A reference clip too long for a model**: by default **Cut it to fit** (at the quietest point before the limit; its transcript is then dropped), or **Refuse it**."],[9616,"A clip whose emotion to borrow"],[11471,"A command"],[9151,"A command runs its job in the foreground in its own process: it does not queue with the server's GPU jobs and loads its own models, so the same model can be loaded in GPU memory twice."],[11711,"A command-line process has no models loaded; the server does"],[9620,"A common parameter `name=value` (repeatable)"],[12035,"a component used outside its phase fails (it was not placed);"],[13402,"A CPU kernel trap found while checking E2-TTS against upstream: `F.linear` on a strided (non-contiguous) 3-D input takes another kernel when the weight requires grad, or when it is an *inference tensor* (made inside `torch.inference_mode()`), even under `no_grad`. Upstream's weights are ordinary parameters that require grad, so native engines leave parameters as `nn.Module` makes them (no `requires_grad_(False)`), and models are loaded outside inference mode. Requests still run inside it. The engine reference has both traps."],[11300,"A database whose schema is newer than the running version is logged (an older Mizuoto shows relative records of a newer one as missing; nothing is deleted)."],[15561,"A dataset is saved in `datasets/<name>/` in the data folder: `dataset.json`, `manifest.jsonl` with one row per clip, and FLAC clips in `audio/`."],[15424,"A description in words (Qwen3-TTS VoiceDesign, VoxCPM2), or choices from fixed attributes (OmniVoice)"],[13508,"A development machine's GPUs may be full with another process's work. Put the engine on the CPU then: `mizuoto config set engines.qwen3tts.device cpu`, or `MIZUOTO_TEST_DEVICE=cpu` for the contract suite. A model always tries to load; when the GPU's memory runs out, the job fails with `compute_unavailable` (exit 9) and every model not in use is unloaded from the GPUs."],[8161,"A device is missing or unusable"],[10643,"A device that does not exist or cannot be used, such as a device naming an unknown remote host"],[8181,"A download failed from every source"],[13231,"a dummy-engine `mizuoto speak`;"],[10911,"A failed capture swaps in a fresh generator in the same state (an aborted capture leaves the old one unusable), and the caller runs eagerly; it is logged once."],[15196,"A failed line does not stop the others: it is marked **Failed** with the reason, and the rest go on."],[10617,"A failing command prints the error and, when the error names a fix, the command to run on the next line; the exit code tells the kind of error. The codes are defined in `mizuoto/core/codes.py`, each error class's exit code in `mizuoto/core/errors.py`:"],[8673,"A failure **while the job runs** raises nothing: `speak(..., wait=True)` returns a job with `state == \"failed\"` and the cause in `job.error` (`code`, `message`, `detail`). What raises is what can be found before running (an unknown model, invalid parameters, a licence not accepted…). The error codes are listed in HTTP API."],[10612,"A few details:"],[15904,"A few GB for torch, plus the models"],[13552,"A few rules across engines are held here too:"],[11478,"A field with a default and a docstring in its group in `core/settings/models.py`; when the UI shows it, a control in Settings, the text in both languages and `typegen`; document it in both language versions of Configuration. A change to `engines.<id>.*` unloads that engine's models, which load with the new settings next time"],[8451,"A file already present with the right size is not downloaded again."],[10655,"A file could not be downloaded from any source"],[8450,"A file is written to `<name>.part` and renamed only when its size and SHA-256 match. Downloading again after an interruption resumes with an HTTP Range request; a server that ignores the range starts the file over."],[13982,"A file the stage made: `sample` for a preview, `checkpoint` for weights"],[15045,"A file's size differs, or a verification failed"],[8473,"A file's size differs, or the last verification failed"],[15642,"A fine-tune needs a GPU in practice. The smallest card each one runs on, with its recipe's default batch, by **Memory** setting (the peaks measured on an RTX 3090, with the estimate's margin: a tenth more and 512 MB):"],[12094,"A fine-tune with a parity fixture's recipe through the whole stack, every stage a child process as in use: each stage's time, the time per step, every metric and the SHA-256 of every weight file the export wrote, compared with an earlier run"],[11611,"A fix to one engine should not wait for, or force, a release of the others. The range is tested at both ends: on Mizuoto at each commit, and on the oldest release it allows"],[8955,"A flow-matching TTS that clones a voice from a short clip and its transcript. Best for: exact control of the generated duration, and replacing a few words of a recording (speech editing)."],[14315,"A flow-matching TTS that fills in a mel spectrogram after the reference's and turns it into audio with Vocos (SWivid/F5-TTS; code MIT, pretrained weights CC-BY-NC-4.0). Code: `mizuoto/engines/f5tts`. On the CPU in fp32 with the same seed it is identical to Mizuoto 0.1 for all three models, cloning and speech editing, and its trainer gives 0.1's exported weights byte for byte. User-facing details: Engines in depth."],[9857,"A folder holding a model"],[15041,"A folder that was not finished, or a shared file it needs is missing"],[8464,"A folder without `model.json` (the download did not finish), or a shared file it needs is missing"],[9156,"A forgotten token is replaced by setting a new one on the server machine."],[14398,"A frame is one slow-transformer step and ten codebooks. The plain loop waited for the device about 22 times a frame: the end-of-turn check; a masked assignment zeroing the codebook embeddings of non-semantic tokens (`vq_sum[~mask] = 0` reads the mask back); the fast transformer's mask and rotary rows taken with list indices (two copies to the device per codebook); a Python boolean stored into a device tensor in the sampler, twice per draw. Each became an exact equivalent (`torch.where`, slices, `fill_`), and the decoding step's mask is made as the one all-true row it is. One wait per frame remains."],[14698,"A frame is one talker step and fifteen code-predictor steps: some 6 000 small kernels, launched one by one by the CPU. The plain loop also waited for the device about 35 times a frame (`torch.multinomial`'s two validity checks per draw, the suppressed ids copied to the device at each step, the padding check, the EOS check), and each wait drained the GPU's queue. `decode.py` removes this without changing a result:"],[13605,"A fresh `torch.Generator` seeded with *s* against the default stream after `torch.manual_seed(s)`"],[13632,"A full request through Mizuoto's stack: native against reference, same seed, same torch"],[13218,"A gated package names the Mizuoto versions it works with in its `pyproject.toml`: `mizuoto>=0.2.0,<0.3`. Its code runs on Mizuoto's runtime and its manifest (options, catalogue, licence) ships in `mizuoto`, so:"],[11817,"A generator: `yield AudioChunk(samples, sample_rate, segment, final)` as soon as each piece is ready, calling `ctx.check_cancel()` at every step; record the values actually used in `ctx.applied` and warnings with `ctx.warn()`"],[8408,"A GPU machine can serve as a remote host from the same image, running `mizuoto agent` instead of the web UI:"],[15555,"a GPU with 24 GB recommended"],[10766,"a hand-written softmax"],[11983,"A handle's **minimum** is its fixed parts plus the copies of its largest units the streamer holds at once."],[11980,"A handle's `kind` decides which units stay resident when not all fit, after the `hot` ones:"],[11260,"A handle's methods are `prepare_voice`, `synthesize` / `convert` / `edit` (generators: the engine runs only inside `next()`, each step with the request context bound and `torch.inference_mode()` entered) and `call(op, payload)` (ASR's `transcribe`, Fish Speech's `codec_*`, `mizuoto.snapshot`). Loading runs outside inference mode. The details are in Runtime."],[8395,"A health check every 30 s on `http://127.0.0.1:7869/api/v1/app/health` (which needs no token)."],[15607,"a histogram of **Clip lengths**;"],[11293,"A host and its remote agents must speak the same protocol version and refuse each other otherwise."],[11283,"A host application can pin values with `settings_overrides`."],[8567,"A Hugging Face compatible address"],[8436,"A Hugging Face mirror, often faster in mainland China"],[10202,"A Hugging Face token, sent to huggingface.co only (never to a mirror) when downloading models"],[16025,"A job card appears at the bottom of the page; when it is done the result is listed under **Results**. Click its play button."],[11481,"A job kind"],[11294,"A job records its process; opening the data folder marks only jobs whose process is gone `interrupted`, so a second command does not interrupt a render in progress."],[13968,"A job worker's stdout (events) and stderr (libraries) reach the host on one pipe, so an event can arrive glued to a progress bar's unfinished `\\r` line. The host splits lines at the event prefix (`parse_lines` in `mizuoto/core/jobs/jsonl.py`); before that, every metric after a progress-bar redraw was lost."],[9193,"A job's log"],[10865,"A kernel that raises (anything but running out of memory or a cancel) is marked broken for that call, and the next backend takes it. Running out of memory propagates to the exact retry. Each fallback is logged once per (site, backend, reason). The request's `Run` counts what it used, and the output records it with a warning when anything fell back:"],[14437,"a larger v2Pro SoVITS"],[9598,"A library voice (id or slug)"],[8323,"A library voice (id or slug); or a preset speaker of the model; or one of OpenAI's names (`alloy`, `ash`, `ballad`, `cedar`, `coral`, `echo`, `fable`, `marin`, `nova`, `onyx`, `sage`, `shimmer`, `verse`), which fall back to the model's own voice, or its first preset speaker when it has no voice of its own. Any other name is 404"],[8250,"A library voice's id or slug"],[10637,"A licence-gated engine (Fish Speech, IndexTTS) whose licence is not accepted yet"],[15408,"A licence-gated engine (Fish Speech, IndexTTS): opens the licence dialog"],[14965,"A licence-gated engine: its distribution, such as `pip install mizuoto-indextts`."],[15059,"A line about the engine. When it is not available, what it needs: **Needs** *torch* (or *mizuoto-indextts*…)**, which is not installed: mizuoto doctor says how to install it.** Every engine is part of Mizuoto except the licence-gated ones, which are packages of their own (see First run)."],[15116,"A line of that speaker (see the rules below)"],[15118,"A line of the narrator"],[11323,"A loaded engine serves one request at a time; a training run holds it too"],[13984,"A log line"],[15150,"a menu:"],[10662,"A missing package looks like this:"],[11706,"A missing transcript is looked up in the cache while planning, else transcribed in the job; without ASR, `clone_no_transcript` or an error with a hint"],[11274,"A missing transcript is transcribed first when `tts.auto_transcribe` is on and ASR is ready (cached by audio SHA-256 and model in the `transcripts` table, and saved into the voice); otherwise the model's `clone_no_transcript` is used, or the request fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command."],[13445,"A Mizuoto development setup has two parts: one Python environment (`.venv`) with torch, Mizuoto installed editable and the development tools, and bun for the web UI and this site. Every engine runs in that one environment; there is nothing else to build. Everyday tasks run through `scripts/dev.py`, which uses only the standard library, behaves the same on Linux, macOS and Windows, and runs the same tools CI runs."],[8321,"A Mizuoto model id; or an alias from `tts.model_aliases`; otherwise `tts.default_model`; with none of them, 404"],[8157,"A model is not downloaded, a package the engine needs is not installed (torch, `mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`; `detail.missing` lists them), a shared file is missing"],[9236,"A model loads on first use, in the server's process, on its engine's device, and stays loaded for the next request:"],[10640,"A model not downloaded; a package the engine needs is not installed (torch, or a licence-gated engine's `mizuoto-fishspeech` / `mizuoto-indextts`); a shared asset missing"],[11897,"A model runs whenever its smallest working set fits the device, not only when all of it fits. Mizuoto's runtime does this the way ComfyUI does (`load_models_gpu`, `ModelPatcher`'s partial loading, dynamic VRAM), without a native allocator: a request places only the components its current step needs; when they do not fit, other components give up memory unit by unit; when that is still not enough, the components load partly and the rest of their weights stream from RAM as each layer runs. Running out of memory becomes slower, not failed."],[9166,"A model that does not fit its GPU loads partly: the layers that fit stay on the GPU and the rest of its weights stream from RAM as they run (slower; the result says so). Mizuoto always tries to load a model, whatever the estimate says, and fails with `compute_unavailable` (exit code 9, HTTP 503; `detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`) only when an allocation really fails. It then unloads every model not in use from every GPU, as ComfyUI does. You can:"],[15402,"A model that is not ready can still be chosen. The **Speak** button at the bottom is then replaced by the **first** thing it needs; click it to start, with its progress:"],[13573,"A model that streams tokens sends its first audio within three quarters of a three-sentence request (GPT-SoVITS v2 with fixed-length chunks: it cuts at pauses by default)"],[13571,"A model that streams: the sink hears its variant's granularity, gets more than one piece of one segment when it streams tokens, and the stored output is the pieces joined"],[15284,"A model unused this long is unloaded"],[9690,"A model with speech editing, e.g. `f5tts/v1-base` (required)"],[9673,"A model with voice conversion, e.g. `cosyvoice/cosyvoice2-0.5b` (required)"],[8133,"A model, voice, job, output or engine is unknown"],[15709,"A model's preset speaker, for that model only"],[9838,"A model's preset speakers"],[8455,"A model's state:"],[11965,"A module may name its units with `memory_units() -> list[nn.Module]`. Otherwise each child of a `ModuleList` or `Sequential` of at least 1 MB is a unit (the outermost lists; a unit is never split further)."],[15441,"A moment after you stop typing, the box shows how Mizuoto will cut long text (**N segments**, one chip each), or **The engine splits long text itself** when the model handles long text. The parameter **Pause between segments (ms)** sets the silence between segments."],[11720,"A name cannot be both a command and a group: `mizuoto env vars`; parameter presets are `--use-preset/-P`, since `--preset` is the preset speaker"],[8137,"A name clash, or a clash with an operation in progress"],[10631,"A name exists already; a stage is running; `webui` finds no free port"],[10782,"a named backend that cannot take a call raises `compute_unavailable` instead of falling back"],[13848,"A new branch, a manual run, a list the compare API cuts short (300 files) or a failure to read it checks everything; `tests/test_ci.py` covers the mapping."],[15114,"A new chapter, titled with the text after `#`"],[14159,"A new CLI command is also added to `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py`."],[15507,"A new dataset"],[15513,"A new experiment"],[15534,"a new model"],[15542,"a new model"],[15550,"a new model"],[15538,"a new model (a CustomVoice model whose preset speaker is the voice)"],[15546,"a new model (a LoRA keeps the base weights beside its adapters)"],[15554,"a new model (still under the Fish Audio research licence)"],[15085,"A new project"],[15109,"A new project starts with one speaker, **Narrator**."],[11453,"A new third-party dependency goes into `pyproject.toml` and into its layer's allowed list in `tests/test_architecture.py`, with the reason it is needed (see Release)."],[15690,"A new voice"],[13873,"A newer run of the same branch cancels the older one. A push to `main` that changes a version file starts the release workflow, which runs `ci.yml` as its checks for what the push changed; CI's own run of that push skips every job (`scope` sees the version file), so the checks run once. Tags start only the release workflow, whose checks are everything. Pushing the docs site to GitHub Pages is `site.yml`'s, not CI's (see Release)."],[9737,"A note about the voice"],[9638,"A parameter preset (`mizuoto preset list`); `--param` and `--option` win over it"],[11699,"A partial mirror works: what it lacks comes from the official repositories file by file, checked against the same SHA-256"],[14785,"A patch is the DiT's Euler steps (each a guidance pair), the local encoder, the stop head and both language models' steps: some 6 000 small kernels, and three waits for the device (the stop flag and each language model's position copied from a Python integer). `model.PatchDecoder` runs a patch over fixed tensors with one wait, for the stop flag. The language models step before the flag is read (upstream reads it first and stops before stepping); they draw nothing and their caches are dropped when generation ends, so the patches are the same. A full cache raises where upstream's step would."],[11697,"A path on one machine means nothing on another"],[9920,"A payload value `key=value` (repeatable)"],[10238,"A PEM certificate (chain): serve HTTPS. Browsers on other machines let a page record the microphone only over HTTPS"],[11920,"A phase of a request; `run` adds the exact retry and the fallback"],[13385,"A phase of the request: its components placed with room for its working memory; `run` adds the exact retry after running out of memory and the optional fallback (Memory)"],[12009,"A phase under `ctx.use` (one that yields audio or consumes a generator) is not retried, so its estimate must bound what it can reach."],[12024,"A phase's estimate decides whether its weights fit whole, so it is sized by the request (its text tokens, batch rows, the reference's length), not by the worst case `max_new_tokens` allows. Setting aside memory the request never uses pushes weights out for nothing: a worst case of 8192 frames, doubled, was 2.4 GB for a Qwen3-TTS sentence that uses about 20 MB."],[11472,"A plain function in `mizuoto/cli/commands/` with `--json`, registered in `get_app()` of `cli/app.py` (name and help at registration), and added to