nes, `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. All three install into one environment over a torch the user chose, and each is versioned, checked and released on its own. This page covers how they are built, checked and published to PyPI (with twine, by the release workflow)."],[11696,"A remote agent owns its models and engines; requests carry files by content (SHA-256); training stays local"],[8185,"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token or speaks another protocol"],[10658,"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token, or speaks another protocol version"],[15999,"A remote host needs the same Mizuoto version as this machine: update both."],[10584,"A remote request whose agent stays silent this long fails (seconds, 10–3600)"],[15732,"a remove button (one clip must remain)."],[15614,"a remove button."],[9360,"A request is batched only when all of these hold:"],[11473,"A route"],[11547,"A route's dependencies are in its signature and tests can pass isolated services; no graph nodes need to share services"],[15635,"A run is one **Train** job whose steps are the stages; its card shows under the stages."],[13956,"A run is one `train` job whose steps are the selected stages:"],[10188,"A running server reads changes to the file within about a second, and open web UIs refresh; saving in the web UI afterwards merges with the file as it is, so it keeps the command line's changes. A broken file makes the server log `Ignored a change to … settings.toml` and keep its settings. `server.host`, `server.port` and the certificates take effect the next time the server starts; changing `engines.<id>.*` unloads that engine's models, which load with the new settings when next used."],[10166,"A sample `settings.toml`"],[13383,"A scratch folder under `<cache>/scratch/<engine>/`, removed when the call ends"],[11485,"A screen"],[13577,"A seeded request gives the same audio before and after another engine's model ran in the process"],[8583,"A server that supports HTTP Range lets interrupted downloads resume."],[11477,"A setting"],[9441,"A short name, used in engine devices (`gpu-box/cuda:0`); not empty, without `/` or `.`"],[11550,"A single user or a small trusted group running it locally; the complexity pays only for multi-tenant serving"],[11837,"A source clip and a voice; a clip, its transcript and `EditSpan`s"],[8449,"A source that answers 401, 403 or 404 for a file, or serves it with the wrong size or SHA-256, is left for the next one at once. Other errors (a dropped connection, a timeout, a 5xx) are retried on the same source up to 4 times, after 1, 2, 4 and 8 seconds (30 at most). When every source fails, the job ends with `download_failed` (exit code 12); its detail lists the sources tried and the last errors. The job log has one line per file naming the source it came from."],[8769,"a speaker"],[15841,"a speaker"],[15189,"A speaker's settings stay when its model (or the project's) changes, so choosing the first model again brings them back. Each line's request carries only the style instruction, parameters and engine options its model takes; the rest are kept but not used. A kept instruction the model does not follow (or not with this voice) says so under the field, and **Add a style instruction** is not offered for that speaker's lines. A preset speaker or a language the new model lacks is marked on the card: those decide what is said, so the lines fail until you choose again."],[11518,"A Stable Diffusion model manager"],[13970,"A stage method returns a JSON-serialisable dict, stored as the stage's `result`; later stages read it from `ctx.results`. `StageContext` (`mizuoto/training/context.py`) offers:"],[11691,"A stage that logs is evidently alive; a silent one still beats"],[15145,"a state dot (hover for the state's name; see the next section);"],[11545,"A static service locator, `ApiDependencies.invoker`"],[14502,"A streamed middle chunk too short for the SOLA overlap leaves an empty piece, on which upstream's post-processing raises an error; kept as upstream behaves. It has been seen with a `min_chunk_length` of 4."],[11984,"A streamed unit's weights rest in RAM. Forward pre- and post-hooks on the unit, and on each module holding its weights, swap `param.data` to a device copy for the call and back after it. Hooks on the leaves make any path into a layer work (`layer.forward_step(…)`, `vae.decode`), and nothing in `ops` or in a layer's code changes. A component wholly on its device has no hooks at all, so the resident path costs nothing."],[8237,"A synthesis can wait for its result: `POST /api/v1/tts/speak?wait=true&timeout=600` answers with the finished job; `result.output_id` (and `result.output_ids` for a batch) is the result's id. When the job is still running after `timeout` seconds (600 by default, at most 3600) the answer is 504 `timeout` with the job in `detail.job_id`; it goes on, and you read it as usual."],[9739,"A tag (repeatable)"],[8850,"A text in a language whose optional extra is missing fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command in the hint, for instance `pip install 'mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]'`."],[13964,"A thread emits a `HeartbeatEvent` every 10 s (`HEARTBEAT_SECONDS`)."],[8177,"A time limit passed (for example `wait=true`)"],[13969,"A trainer is a `mizuoto.training.Trainer` subclass with one `stage_<id>(ctx)` method per stage id its methods declare; `ctx.request[\"method\"]` says which method runs. The trainer's module imports no torch at the top: the host imports it to read `REQUIRES` and `DEVICES` (`InferenceService.trainer_needs`) and to ask `refuses(method, model_dir)`, which says, without torch, why a method cannot start from a model (Qwen3-TTS: the 0.6B Base for `speaker`; the method then shows as unavailable, and a run cannot start), so the maths lives in modules it imports inside the stage methods. CosyVoice's trainer, for example, sets `DEVICES = (\"cuda\", \"cpu\")`: upstream trains under torchrun on CUDA only, and nothing in the native port needs CUDA."],[13889,"A training method is `[training.<id>]` in the engine's manifest (`TrainingMethod`). OmniVoice's LoRA:"],[11688,"A training run is one `train` job whose steps are its stages, each stage a child process; the stages are declared statically in the manifest"],[10786,"A training stage binds its policy process-wide (`dispatch.PROCESS_POLICY`), because autograd runs backward passes, and gradient checkpointing's recomputed forwards, on threads of its own."],[8169,"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering"],[10649,"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering; the engine raised an exception"],[11713,"A tunnel's or proxy's visitors must not browse the server's disk"],[11964,"A unit is a group of weights that moves together: a decoder layer, a DiT block, a vocoder stage (ComfyUI's dynamic-VRAM units)."],[12036,"a unit's weight read outside its `forward` fails (it is not there)."],[11627,"A user's output should not change because the implementation did; where 0.1 differed from upstream on purpose (F5-TTS generating chunks in order rather than on a thread pool), 0.1 is the reference"],[10205,"A value that parses as JSON is used as JSON (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), else as a string; `null` or `none` means empty."],[11769,"A variant is a set of static capabilities; requests are validated against it before any job exists:"],[15707,"A voice a design model made from a description; the clip it spoke becomes its main clip, so other models can clone it too"],[9656,"A voice attribute `key=value` (repeatable)"],[9754,"A voice attribute `key=value` (repeatable)"],[9608,"A voice attribute `key=value` (repeatable), such as OmniVoice's `gender=female`"],[9652,"A voice design model (required)"],[9750,"A voice design model (required)"],[14665,"A voice from a free-text description"],[15418,"A voice from the voice library"],[8252,"A voice given with the request, in one way only: `references` (`[{\"au