63,"all four"],[10156,"All settings"],[14328,"All three clone (the reference's transcript is required) and edit speech. The model folder holds the checkpoint (`*.safetensors`, else `*.pt`), `vocab.txt` and `vocos/config.yaml` + `vocos/pytorch_model.bin`. E2's repository has no vocabulary, so upstream's bundled `vocab.txt` ships with the engine as package data and serves it."],[12599,"all; and on `cuda:1` identical to G0's `cuda:0`"],[12049,"also AdamW's state in RAM, stepped on the CPU (`host_optimizer`; Qwen3-TTS, OmniVoice, F5-TTS without a gradient scaler); VoxCPM's LoRA base weights streamed from RAM for each product (`streamed_linear`)"],[9662,"Also copy the result here"],[9679,"Also copy the result here"],[9696,"Also copy the result here"],[9596,"Also copy the result here; its extension picks the format"],[10704,"always"],[12052,"Always: a GPU stage reports `memory/peak_mb`; `MethodInfo.memory_mb` estimates a run's peak per preset (`core/training/estimate.py`): every method was measured on an RTX 3090 with its recipe's default batch, each installed base model and each preset; an estimate is the nearest measured model's peak scaled by size, a tenth more and 512 MB for the CUDA context, and for Fish Speech, GPT-SoVITS and VoxCPM, whose peaks follow the batch, the run's `batch_size` against the measured one. A GPU run warns in its log when the estimate exceeds the free memory, naming the preset that would fit or, where none does, the largest batch that would. Trainers themselves are in Trainers."],[13195,"AMD (ROCm; `cuda` to torch)"],[7997,"AMD、Intel、Apple 芯片和纯 CPU 的 torch 构建，以及从源码或用 Docker 安装，见安装。"],[5178,"AMD（ROCm，torch 里也叫 `cuda`）"],[15522,"An **experiment**: a model to start from and a way to train it, run on the dataset stage by stage with the engine's own fine-tuning recipe, implemented in Mizuoto. The result is **a voice's own weights** (added to a voice in the library) or **a new model** (listed under **Models**)."],[11476,"An `EventBase` subclass (`__event_name__`) in `core/events/models.py`; it enters the OpenAPI schema by itself. Regenerate the types and handle it in the UI's `api/socket.ts`"],[8348,"An agent in a container"],[11521,"An AI image browser on the same skeleton"],[10990,"An API that can delete and move files checks three things on every HTTP and WebSocket request (before any route; plain ASGI):"],[10740,"An architecture test forbids `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` and its aten kernels anywhere outside `runtime/accel/`."],[9705,"An audio file"],[10906,"An autoregressive model on a GPU launches thousands of small kernels per step (Qwen3-TTS: about 6 000 per 80 ms frame), and every wait for the device drains the queue, so the CPU's launch time and the GPU's work add up instead of overlapping. Each decoder now waits for the device once per frame or token, and with `compute.cuda_graphs` (on by default; NVIDIA only, ROCm's HIP graphs unchecked) its step's kernels are captured once and replayed at once. A graph replays exactly the kernels the eager code launched, with the same arguments, so its results are the eager code's bit for bit."],[13976,"An effective hyperparameter, `default` when `None`"],[9614,"An emotion weight `name=value` (repeatable)"],[11261,"An engine has two parts: a **manifest** (`mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/<id>.toml`, package data shipped in the wheel) and an **implementation** (a subclass of `mizuoto.runtime.engine.Engine`)."],[11740,"An engine in Mizuoto is two things in two places, plus its tests:"],[11848,"An engine is *available* when torch imports (the dummy engine needs none) and its implementation is registered; otherwise `EngineStatus.missing` names what is missing and the UI and `mizuoto doctor` show the fix."],[11789,"An engine is a package under `mizuoto/engines/<id>/` whose `__init__.py` exports the `Engine` subclass, and whose modules import only what the layer rules allow: `mizuoto.runtime`, `mizuoto.nn`, `mizuoto.text`, `mizuoto.training`, `mizuoto.core.codes`, `mizuoto.core.inference.tasks`, its own package, and numpy, torch and the text libraries; never another engine. Its module imports no torch at the top (`test_engine_contract_import_is_light` and `test_manifest_options_match_the_engines` import engine modules without torch): torch is imported inside the methods, and type hints go under `if TYPE_CHECKING:`."],[11968,"An engine marks submodules on the handle with `handle.mark(module, mark)`:"],[9159,"An engine needs torch (only the dummy engine runs without it) and its implementation: every engine is built into Mizuoto except Fish Speech and IndexTTS, which are distributions of their own. The engine card and `mizuoto doctor <engine>` say what is missing:"],[9465,"An engine on a remote host is marked **On gpu-box** (the host's name) on its engine card and model rows, with the hints **Its packages are gpu-box’s: mizuoto doctor qwen3tts there** for the engine and **These are the models on gpu-box: download them there with mizuoto model download** for its models."],[11479,"An engine option"],[9622,"An engine option `name=value` (repeatable)"],[11483,"An engine or a trainer"],[8173,"An engine raised an exception"],[11828,"An engine returns float32 mono audio in `[-1, 1]` at the model's own rate and never encodes: joining, normalising, resampling and encoding are the core's job. It receives resolved, absolute paths that exist (references are 16-bit WAV in `cache/refs/`) and never downloads. The core has validated the request against the manifest, so an engine maps rather than checks."],[9259,"An engine serves one request at a time on a device; the next waits (**Waiting for the engine**). A job waiting for a GPU another job holds shows **Waiting for the GPU**; when the memory suffices for both, **Run anyway** in **Jobs** starts it beside the other, or raise `compute.gpu_jobs`. A fine-tune takes the whole GPU, whatever `compute.gpu_jobs` says, and the idle models on it move to RAM first."],[11275,"An engine whose device is `<host>/<device>` runs on that host's `mizuoto agent`. The agent is a whole Mizuoto: its own data folder, models and engines, in its own process."],[11933,"An engine with `PHASED = True` (every real engine Mizuoto ships; the dummy is not) wraps each part of a request in a phase, so only that part's components are placed, with that part's working memory set aside:"],[11937,"An engine without `PHASED` gets every handle for the whole call, with `memory_required(task)` as the working memory."],[13334,"An engine's `DEVICES` (every kind by default) mirror its manifest's `devices`; `torch.compile` runs eagerly on MPS."],[11265,"An engine's `OPTION_SCHEMA` must equal its manifest's `[options]`, and `Engine.DEVICES` its manifest's `devices` (`tests/core/test_engines.py` checks both); the engine's `detect_variant()` (files only, no torch) gives the same variant as `core/models/detect.py`, which the host uses when importing a model."],[9900,"An engine's variants, capabilities, parameters and models"],[8120,"An error answers with its HTTP status and one shape:"],[11475,"An event"],[15129,"An example:"],[13951,"An experiment is `experiments/<engine>/<name>/`: `experiment.json` (base model, dataset, method, hyperparameters, stage states), the trainer's work folder `work/`, and `metrics.jsonl`."],[10006,"An experiment is named `<engine>/<name>`, or just its name when that is unique."],[15624,"An experiment is saved in `experiments/<engine>/<name>/`."],[15110,"An imported script is plain text, with these rules (the hint under the box says the same):"],[13171,"An in-tree Whisper, log-mel and the `tiktoken` vocabulary (shipped)"],[9114,"An internal engine Mizuoto uses itself: Whisper large-v3-turbo, implemented in Mizuoto, about 100 languages, transcribing reference clips, voices and datasets that have no text. It is not offered as a speech model and does not appear in `GET /v1/models`."],[10634,"An invalid request: the model lacks that voice mode or parameter, a reference clip is too short 