 chain"],[11230,"Background"],[10793,"Backward"],[15400,"Badges under the model list its capabilities, such as **Clone a voice**, **Preset speakers**, **Instructions**, **Streaming** and **Long text**."],[8872,"Base (cloning)"],[8877,"Base (cloning)"],[8351,"Base image"],[855,"Base（克隆）"],[860,"Base（克隆）"],[10598,"Batches and parameters"],[14572,"Beam sampling used to wait for the device about ten times a step (`torch.multinomial`'s checks, the scorer reading each candidate with `.item()`, the stopping test, the beam reorder, the position embedding's index tensor). Now once: the draw is `multinomial`'s own `topk(p / Exp(1), 2 × beams)` (`runtime.sampling.multinomial_draws`, the same ids and generator state on the CPU and CUDA); the candidates' scores, tokens and beams are read back together and the scorer decides on the host from those values; the position embedding is its table's row. With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the GPT wholly on its device, with a KV cache: IndexTTS 2/2.5, and 1.5 in fp16) the GPT-2's one-token steps of all beams run as graphs around each layer's attention; the cache, its beam reorder and the sampling stay eager. The same audio, 2.6–3.2 times faster per step on the 1.5's sizes. The beams' keys and values for every layer share one buffer (`BeamCaches`), which a step grows by a position with the beams' rows reordered in one copy per beam, each layer then writing its new key and value in place: each layer's keys and values are the contiguous tensors `index_select` and `torch.cat` made before, at half the copying (×1.11 on 30 s of speech)."],[8197,"Bearer header"],[180,"Bearer 头"],[12268,"before"],[12284,"before"],[12328,"before"],[12342,"before"],[12397,"before"],[12354,"Before"],[12368,"Before"],[12182,"Before → after"],[13415,"Before each phase of a call, idle components on the same device give up memory, unit by unit, to make room; what does not fit streams from RAM (Memory)"],[12588,"before round 1 → round 1 (`8a021de`)"],[8666,"Behaviour"]