07,"Command"],[9816,"Command"],[9825,"Command"],[9840,"Command"],[9865,"Command"],[9893,"Command"],[9902,"Command"],[9924,"Command"],[9940,"Command"],[9973,"Command"],[10007,"Command"],[10038,"Command"],[10053,"Command"],[10085,"Command"],[10100,"Command"],[15229,"Command"],[14992,"Command line"],[15030,"Command line"],[15097,"Command line"],[15397,"Command line"],[15519,"Command line"],[15699,"Command line"],[8335,"Command line: the same operations in a terminal."],[9530,"Command reference"],[10678,"Command reference: every command's arguments and options."],[14160,"Commit and open PRs only when asked."],[11436,"Commit messages"],[11495,"Commit messages take the form `type(scope): summary`, the summary in lower case, saying what the change does:"],[8256,"Common parameters: `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`, `speed`, `seed`, `segment_silence_ms`…"],[9125,"Common questions by topic: starting up, the access token, torch and engines, GPU memory, licences, downloads, logs and remote hosts."],[10594,"Common workflows"],[13597,"Compares the two implementations' training runs; the exported voice or model can be handed to the other implementation to load"],[13593,"Compares two runs sample for sample (`--tolerance`, `--report` writes a Markdown report); prints the current table from the fixtures without running a model"],[12725,"Compile cost"],[9322,"Compiled"],[10889,"Compiled module"],[9213,"Compiling models (`compute.compile`)"],[13413,"Components"],[12001,"Components in use by any request are never victims; the running model's components that the current phase does not need are. Each victim gives up units, in reverse fill order, until the shortfall is met (`partially_unload`); in `high` and `shared` it leaves whole. `empty_cache` runs after an eviction, never per request."],[11936,"Components the phase does not name stay where they are and give up memory first when another phase needs it: an IndexTTS clone of a cached voice never places w2v-BERT or CAM++."],[47,"compute"],[8064,"compute"],[15255,"Compute"],[11842,"Compute attention with `mizuoto.runtime.accel.attention(q, k, v, site=SITE, …)`, never `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` (an architecture test forbids it): declare `SITE = accel.Site(\"<id>.<part>\")` once per call site, and pass the arguments upstream passed to SDPA (`causal` is its `is_causal`). A site where upstream wrote attention by hand gives that code as its `reference`; one that only its reference may compute is `swappable=False` (attentions with relative positions inside the scores are not sites at all: they stay hand-written). Where the site builds a mask from a structure (padding on one side, causal, a window), pass `mask_info` too, so faster kernels can take the call (Acceleration)."],[12062,"Conditions"],[12264,"Configuration"],[10149,"Configuration and environment variables"],[10679,"Configuration and environment variables: settings, environment variables and the data folder."],[10560,"Connect with TLS"],[10975,"Contents"],[15568,"Contents"],[15976,"Contents"],[11427,"Conventions"],[14119,"Conventions that hold everywhere"],[11051,"Conventions:"],[15480,"Convert voice"],[182,"Cookie"],[8199,"Cookie"],[13367,"Cooperative cancel. `check_cancel()` raises `Cancelled`, a `BaseException`, so model code's `except Exception` cannot swallow it. Engines call it at every token or ODE step"],[11991,"Copies are made outside inference mode, in the weights' own dtype, so a streamed layer computes with the same kind of tensor as a resident one (an inference tensor takes other CPU kernels). Each fetch checks for a cancel. A `Compiled` module above a streamed unit runs eagerly (its graph would hold the weights), and CUDA graphs are captured for models wholly on their device, or for a `sequence` handle whose streamed units rest in page-locked memory (`ModelHandle.graphable`; Qwen3-TTS's talker uses it). Captured, each streamed weight's copy is a memcpy node from its fixed host tensor into the graph's own memory, made inside the capture (a copy from the eager run before it is not used: the graph would keep reading that buffer after it is freed) and per leaf, so a layer split across graphs around its attention copies each weight once a step. The streamer counts the replays' copies (`ModelHandle.replayed`), so `meta.memory.streamed_mb` stays right."],[10327,"Copy streams for streamed weights (-1: two on NVIDIA and AMD, none elsewhere; 0: off); autoregressive models never prefetch"],[9290,"copy streams that move streamed weights while the GPU computes (`-1`: two on NVIDIA and AMD, none elsewhere); used for models that run once per input, not for autoregressive ones, where they only cost memory"],[11059,"Core method"],[13636,"Corpus runs in each engine's production dtype and device, native against reference; seeds not aligned (GPU kernels differ)"],[9791,"Correct a clip's transcript"],[10001,"Correct, exclude or delete a clip"],[13626,"Cosine ≥ 0.999"],[729,"CosyVoice"],[1308,"CosyVoice"],[2875,"CosyVoice"],[5087,"CosyVoice"],[5917,"CosyVoice"],[6185,"CosyVoice"],[6819,"CosyVoice"],[7050,"CosyVoice"],[7827,"CosyVoice"],[8746,"CosyVoice"],[9325,"CosyVoice"],[10892,"CosyVoice"],[13104,"CosyVoice"],[13934,"CosyVoice"],[14202,"CosyVoice"],[14836,"CosyVoice"],[15067,"CosyVoice"],[15843,"CosyVoice"],[8771,"CosyVoice (`cosyvoice`)"],[15548,"CosyVoice (300M, 2, 3)"],[8918,"CosyVoice 1 (300M)"],[909,"CosyVoice 1 Instruct"],[8926,"CosyVoice 1 Instruct"],[8922,"CosyVoice 1 SFT (preset speakers)"],[13691,"CosyVoice 1 SFT, presets"],[5674,"CosyVoice 1 SFT，预置说话人"],[905,"CosyVoice 1 SFT（预置说话人）"],[901,"CosyVoice 1（300M）"],[896,"CosyVoice 2"],[4843,"CosyVoice 2"],[4959,"CosyVoice 2"],[8913,"CosyVoice 2"],[12860,"CosyVoice 2"],[12976,"CosyVoice 2"],[5037,"CosyVoice 2 / 3"],[13054,"CosyVoice 2 / 3"],[13022,"CosyVoice 2 / 3 (1.5 GB)"],[12925,"CosyVoice 2 / 3 (fp32 sites)"],[12877,"CosyVoice 2 / 3 `llm` (and 2's `llm_flow`)"],[4860,"CosyVoice 2 / 3 `llm`（以及 2 的 `llm_flow`）"],[7631,"CosyVoice 2 / 3, `llm` （2 的 `llm_f