 work and largest estimate can come from different calls, such as a reference's encoding and a decoding)."],[14067,"Media URLs (`urls.output()`, `urls.audioFile()`) are fetched by `<audio>` directly and authenticated by the `mizuoto_token` cookie; uploads use `uploadRaw()` (XMLHttpRequest, for progress; the body is raw bytes)."],[14933,"Mel filterbanks, kaldi fbank, resamplers, WAV and FLAC, the tiled decoding used as a memory fallback"],[6916,"mel 滤波器组、kaldi fbank、重采样器、WAV 和 FLAC、用作显存回退的分块解码"],[11790,"Member"],[13364,"Member"],[13971,"Member"],[11881,"Memory"],[13291,"Memory"],[13884,"Memory"],[14167,"Memory"],[14645,"Memory"],[14209,"Memory and speed"],[14311,"Memory and speed"],[14367,"Memory and speed"],[14417,"Memory and speed"],[14509,"Memory and speed"],[14586,"Memory and speed"],[14722,"Memory and speed"],[12080,"Memory estimates calibrated"],[13409,"Memory is managed at three levels:"],[13555,"Memory management changes where weights live, not what is computed, so a partly loaded or streamed model must give exactly what a whole one gives. `tests/engines_native/streaming.py` lets the CPU play a device of a given size (`DeviceService(simulate=…, strict=True)`):"],[13559,"Memory management itself is in Memory management."],[12083,"Memory modes and a real out-of-memory"],[11639,"Merging would make CosyVoice need a gated engine's licence; the emotion model lives inside each model's repository folder, and sharing it would mean moving installed models' files"],[11809,"Method"],[13338,"Method"],[13911,"Method"],[14352,"Method `full` (stages `prepare`, `train`, `export`): upstream's `finetune_cli` recipe, without accelerate, datasets, wandb or ema_pytorch. Seeded alike, it gives 0.1's losses, learning rates and exported `model_<update>.safetensors` byte for byte on the CPU. (0.1 itself never seeded: its condition drops came from an unseeded `random`.)"],[14400,"Method `lora` (stages `tokens`, `train`, `export`): upstream's `extract_vq`, `build_dataset`, its Lightning + Hydra `train.py` with loralib and `merge_lora`, without any of those libraries or protobuf. Seeded alike, it gives 0.1's codes, losses, LoRA weights and exported `model.pth` bit for bit on the CPU, and every other exported file byte for byte. (0.1 never seeded, so only its first step repeats.) It runs on every device kind."],[14705,"Method `speaker` (Base models; stages `prepare`, `train`, `export`): the model learns one speaker and becomes a CustomVoice model whose only preset speaker is the new voice, as upstream's `finetuning/sft_12hz.py`. On the real 1.7B Base, seeded alike, it gives 0.1's codes, losses and checkpoint byte for byte on the CPU, without transformers or accelerate."],[14493,"Method `speaker` (stages `text`, `speech`, `semantic`, `sovits`, `gpt`, `export`): upstream's own recipe, without Lightning, torchmetrics, transformers, pandas or the ffmpeg program. The export is the voice's own pair of weights."],[9508,"Method and path"],[15525,"Methods"],[14788,"Methods `full` and `lora` (`train.py`, the maths in `sft.py`), upstream's `train_voxcpm_finetune.py` with its per-model recipes (`conf/<model>/*.yaml`), which fill any hyperparameter left at 0. No `datasets`, `transformers`, `argbind` or tensorboard. Stages: `prepare` (the clips at the VAE's rate, read as `datasets` reads them: soundfile's float64 and `librosa.resample`'s soxr; their tokens; the `max_batch_tokens` filter), `train`, `export`."],[14628,"Methods `full` and `lora` (stages `tokens`, `train`, `export`; upstream's `extract_audio_tokens` and `OmniTrainer` with its SDPA fine-tune configurations; no transformers, peft, accelerate or webdataset). Seeded alike, both give 0.1's codes, batches, losses, learning rates, LoRA adapter and exported `model.safetensors` byte for byte on the CPU, also with gradient accumulation and over several shards and loader workers. The LoRA is merged into the exported model."],[14287,"Methods `llm` and `llm_flow` (stages `features`, `llm`, `flow`, `export`; from CosyVoice 1, 2 or 3): upstream's LibriTTS recipe and `bin/train.py`, without onnxruntime, pyarrow, pyworld, transformers, deepspeed or torchrun. It gives upstream's losses, accuracies, learning rates and `epoch_<N>_whole.pt` byte for byte on the CPU (gloo, world size 1), for all three generations, with zero or two loader workers and an accumulation left over at an epoch's end; the features (speech tokens and CAM++) give onnxruntime's tokens and its embeddings within 6e-6. Upstream trains on CUDA only; the trainer runs on every device kind."],[8598,"Methods and properties"],[11118,"Micro-batching"],[10987,"Middleware, in order: an optional `CORSMiddleware` (only when `server.allowed_origins` is non-empty), `GZipMiddleware` (above 4 KB) and `SecurityMiddleware`. The lifespan only starts and stops the socket bridge."],[14755,"MiniCPM-4: RMSNorm, LongRoPE, GQA SDPA, the static KV cache, muP residuals"],[6738,"MiniCPM-4：RMSNorm、LongRoPE、GQA SDPA、静态 KV 缓存、muP 残差"],[774,"MIT"],[809,"MIT"],[7841,"MIT"],[8791,"MIT"],[8826,"MIT"],[15857,"MIT"],[8784,"MIT code, CC-BY-NC-4.0 weights"],[15852,"MIT code; CC-BY-NC-4.0 weights"],[11629,"Mixing fixes with porting makes a parity failure ambiguous; identical behaviour is the default, and a deviation needs a reason and a record"],[3526,"Mizuoto"],[7776,"Mizuoto"],[11543,"Mizuoto"],[15792,"Mizuoto"],[3509,"Mizuoto 0.1"],[11526,"Mizuoto 0.1"],[11647,"Mizuoto 0.1 never had VoxCPM"],[3630,"Mizuoto 0.1 没有 VoxCPM"],[3512,"Mizuoto 0.2"],[11529,"Mizuoto 0.2"],[14124,"Mizuoto 0.2 is one Python distribution installed into one environment. Every engine (Qwen3-TTS, F5-TTS, OmniVoice, CosyVoice, GPT-SoVITS, VoxCPM, Fish Speech, IndexTTS and the internal Whisper ASR) is implemented in Mizuoto on its own runtime and runs **in the server's own process**. There is no upstream code, no transformers, no environment per engine and no worker process."],[6107,"Mizuoto 0.2 是装进同一个 Python 环境的一个发行包。每个引擎（Qwen3-TTS、F5-TTS、OmniVoice、CosyVoice、GPT-SoVITS、VoxCPM、Fish Speech、IndexTTS，以及内部使用的 Whisper 语音识别）都在 Mizuoto 里基于它自己的运行时实现，**在服务器自己的进程里**运行。没有上游代码，没有 transformers，没有引擎专用环境，也没有 worker 进程。"],[9157,"Mizuoto does not require one, but set one. With `mizuoto webui --host 0.0.0.0` the server only logs \"Binding to 0.0.0.0 makes the server reachable from other machines.\" and stops checking the `Host` header; without a token, anyone who can reach the address can do everything (download models, delete outputs…). Reading server paths and showing files in a folder stay limited to a browser on the server's own machine."],[8482,"Mizuoto identifies the engine and variant from the folder's files (and a GPT-SoVITS weight's version). A folder it does not recognise is refused."],[15910,"Mizuoto is on PyPI as `mizuoto`; the licence-gated engines are `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. Use a virtual environment of your choice. Install torch first, from the index that matches your machine, so that installing Mizuoto keeps that build:"],[13131,"Mizuoto is one environment: the dependencies of the core, the API, the command line, the web UI and every engine are in `pyproject.toml` and install at once. Every new dependency must answer three questions: does it have wheels for every platform CI covers (Linux x86_64, Windows x86_64, macOS arm64, CPython 3.10–3.13), does it change results, does it change process-wide state."],[15894,"Mizuoto is one Python distribution: the server, the web UI, the command line and every engine run in one Python environment. Install **torch** first, in the build for your hardware, then **Mizuoto**. The two licence-gated engines (Fish Speech, IndexTTS) are distributions of their own, installed beside Mizuoto when you want them."],[10150,"Mizuoto keeps its settings in settings.toml, and the web UI's Settings, the mizuoto config command and MIZUOTO_ environment variables all change the same settings; this page lists every setting, the environment variables and the data folder's layout."],[9233,"Mizuoto looks for GPUs without loading torch: `nvidia-smi` for NVIDIA cards, `rocm-smi` (or `amd-smi`) for AMD cards, which torch's ROCm build names `cuda:0`, `cuda:1`… like NVIDIA's, and Apple silicon by the platform (`mps`). `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` applies to what `nvidia-smi` finds as it does to torch: only the cards it names (indices or `GPU-` UUIDs), numbered from `cuda:0` in its order (indices are `nvidia-smi`'s, in PCI bus order: set `CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID` if your cards differ). When none of these finds a GPU but the installed torch is a build that could use one (the XPU build for Intel GPUs, a ROCm build without `rocm-smi`, a CUDA build in a container without `nvidia-smi`), Mizuoto asks torch in a separate process once (a second or two); a CPU build of torch is never asked. Once Mizuoto has loaded torch to run a model, torch's own figures are used. `mizuoto doctor` lists the GPUs found and how, and **Settings** › **Compute** shows them."],[9263,"Mizuoto manages GPU memory as ComfyUI does. A request places only the parts of a model it needs for each step (a voice prompt's encoder, then the language model, then the vocoder), and the parts it does not need give up their memory first when another needs it. When a model does not fit at all, it loads **partly**: the layers that fit stay on the GPU and the rest of its weights stay in RAM, copied to the GPU as each layer runs. It is slower, and it runs instead of failing."],[15797,"Mizuoto puts open text-to-speech engines — CosyVoice, F5-TTS, GPT-SoVITS, OmniVoice, Qwen3-TTS, VoxCPM, Fish Speech and IndexTTS — into **one platform**: one local server, one web UI and one command line, `mizuoto`. Use it to speak text, clone and design voices, have a cast of voices read a whole book or script, convert and edit recordings, and fine-tune models on your own recordings."],[11513,"Mizuoto was not designed from nothing. Its application skeleton (core services, thin API and command line, a Vue UI shipped in the wheel, the tooling) comes from a line of sibling projects, and its model runtime follows ComfyUI. This page records what was taken from each source and why, what was deliberately left out, and finally the design decisions that shaped the code as it is. What the code looks like is in Architecture."],[15053,"Mizuoto works out the engine and variant from the files:"],[1140,"Mizuoto 不强制要求，但请设置一个。`mizuoto webui --host 0.0.0.0` 时服务器只在日志里警告 \"Binding to 0.0.0.0 makes the server reachable from other machines.\"，不再检查 `Host` 头；没有令牌时，任何能连到这个地址的人都能使用全部功能（下载模型、删除结果等）。读取服务器上的路径、在文件夹中显示等操作始终只对服务器本机的浏览器开放。"],[3496,"Mizuoto 不是从零设计的。它的应用骨架（核心服务、薄的 API 与命令行、随 wheel 发布的 Vue 界面、工具链）来自一系列同源项目，模型运行时借鉴 ComfyUI。本页记录这些来源里哪些被采用、为什么采用、哪些有意没有采用，最后列出塑造了现在这套代码的设计决策及其理由。代码是什么样的，见整体架构。"],[6395,"Mizuoto 中 GPT-SoVITS 引擎的实现：v2、v2Pro、v2ProPlus、v4 和 v5 Turbo，带有移植的转换器和模型的文本前端，T2S 模型、SoVITS 与流模型，哪些做法与上游完全一致，GPU 解码，写出上游文件的音色微调，以及对照结果。"],[6700,"Mizuoto 中 VoxCPM 引擎的实现：VoxCPM2、1.5 和 0.5B，MiniCPM-4、局部 DiT 与 AudioVAE，按上游锁定的库版本构建的分词器和文本规范化，哪些做法与上游完全一致，带 CUDA 图的逐块解码，全量与 LoRA 微调，以及对照结果。"],[6186,"Mizuoto 中实现的 CosyVoice 引擎：CosyVoice 1、2、3，由 ONNX 文件构建的语音分词器和 CAM++，语言模型、flow 与 HiFT，哪些做法与上游完全一致、为什么完整链路不是逐位一致，GPU 解码路径，LLM 与 flow 微调，以及对照结果。"],[6289,"Mizuoto 中实现的 F5-TTS 引擎：v1 Base、v0 Base 和 E2，DiT 与 UNetT，CFM 采样器与 Vocos，哪些做法与上游完全一致，显存与编译说明，全量微调，以及对照结果。"],[6564,"Mizuoto 中实现的 OmniVoice 引擎：迭代解掩码的双向 Qwen3，HiggsAudio v2 分词器（DAC 与 HuBERT），不依赖 pydub 的 pydub 算术，哪些做法与上游完全一致，全量与 LoRA 微调，以及对照结果。"],[6623,"Mizuoto 中实现的 Qwen3-TTS 引擎：变体与文件，talker、code predictor、说话人编码器和 12 Hz 编解码器，哪些做法与上游完全一致，显存与 CUDA 图解码，说话人微调，以及对照结果。"],[302,"Mizuoto 中的处理"],[1246,"Mizuoto 像 ComfyUI 一样管理显存。一个请求的每一步只放上它需要的模型部分（先是参考音频的编码器，然后是语言模型，再是声码器），不需要的部分在别处需要显存时先让出。模型完全放不下时，**部分加载**：放得下的层留在 GPU 上，其余权重留在内存中，每层运行时再复制到 GPU。这样更慢，但能运行而不是失败。"],[385,"Mizuoto 写入的一切都在 `/data` 中：`settings.toml`、数据库、模型、共享文件、音色、结果、数据集、实验、项目、缓存和日志。镜像本身不保存状态，重新构建的镜像可以继续使用同一个数据卷。"],[6345,"Mizuoto 单独发行包 mizuoto-fishspeech 中实现的 Fish Speech S2 Pro 引擎：双自回归 transformer 与 44.1 kHz 编解码器，哪些做法与上游完全一致，每帧只等待设备一次与 CUDA 图，LoRA 微调，以及对照结果。"],[6487,"Mizuoto 单独发行包 mizuoto-indextts 中实现的 IndexTTS 引擎：IndexTTS-1.5、2 和 2.5，带束采样的 GPT-2、条件编码、情感与 s2mel 解码器，哪些做法与上游完全一致，显存与 GPU 解码，以及对照结果。"],[2270,"Mizuoto 可以使用的设备，如 `[\"cuda:0\"]`；为空时使用找到的全部设备"],[1212,"Mizuoto 可以使用的设备，如 `[\"cuda:0\"]`；空为全部"],[2570,"mizuoto 命令行与网页界面、HTTP 接口调用同一个核心：本页介绍它的共同约定、前台任务、退出码，以及在服务器运行时使用它。"],[7894,"Mizuoto 在 PyPI 上的包名是 `mizuoto`；需要接受许可的引擎是 `mizuoto-fishspeech` 和 `mizuoto-indextts`。请在你自己选择的虚拟环境中安装。先从适合本机的索引安装 torch，这样安装 Mizuoto 时会保留这个构建："],[3834,"Mizuoto 对移植的标准是：在 CPU 上以 fp32、带种子运行时，输出与上游实现完全相同。对于 Mizuoto 0.1 已有的引擎，`scripts/parity/` 让同样的用例分别走 0.1 的链路和原生链路，逐采样比较（见测试）。移植复现了什么、哪里有偏差、对照结果如何，记在引擎参考中该引擎的页面（`site/content/docs/engines-<id>.mdx` 与 `.en.mdx`）；以后的改动不能破坏的规则记在 `AGENTS.md`。"],[7781,"Mizuoto 把多款开源语音合成（TTS）引擎——CosyVoice、F5-TTS、GPT-SoVITS、OmniVoice、Qwen3-TTS、VoxCPM、Fish Speech 和 IndexTTS——放进**一个平台**：同一个本地服务器、同一个网页界面和同一个命令行工具 `mizuoto`。你可以用它合成语音、克隆与设计音色、让一组角色朗读整本书或剧本、转换与编辑录音，并用自己的录音微调模型。"],[7878,"Mizuoto 是一个 Python 发行包：服务器、网页界面、命令行和所有引擎都在同一个 Python 环境中运行。先安装适合本机硬件的 **torch**，再安装 **Mizuoto**。两个需要接受许可的引擎（Fish Speech、IndexTTS）是单独的发行包，需要时与 Mizuoto 装在一起。"],[5114,"Mizuoto 是一个环境：核心、API、命令行、Web UI 和每个引擎的依赖都写在 `pyproject.toml` 里，一次安装。每个新依赖都要回答：它在 CI 覆盖的每个平台（Linux x86_64、Windows x86_64、macOS arm64，CPython 3.10–3.13）上有没有 wheel，它会不会改变结果，它会不会改动进程级状态。"],[1216,"Mizuoto 查找 GPU 时不加载 torch：NVIDIA 显卡用 `nvidia-smi`；AMD 显卡用 `rocm-smi`（或 `amd-smi`），torch 的 ROCm 构建与 NVIDIA 一样把它们命名为 `cuda:0`、`cuda:1`……；Apple 芯片按平台识别（`mps`）。`CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` 对 `nvidia-smi` 找到的显卡与对 torch 一样生效：只保留它列出的显卡（序号或 `GPU-` UUID），按它的顺序从 `cuda:0` 编号（序号是 `nvidia-smi` 的，按 PCI 总线顺序：显卡型号不同时请设置 `CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID`）。这些都找不到 GPU、而已安装的 torch 是能使用 GPU 的构建时（Intel 显卡的 XPU 构建、没有 `rocm-smi` 的 ROCm 构建、容器里没有 `nvidia-smi` 的 CUDA 构建），Mizuoto 会在单独的进程里询问一次 torch（一两秒）；CPU 构建的 torch 不会被询问。Mizuoto 为运行模型加载了 torch 之后，改用 torch 自己的数据。`mizuoto doctor` 会列出找到的 GPU 及查找方式，**设置** › **计算** 中也会显示。"],[7036,"Mizuoto 根据文件判断它属于哪个引擎、哪个变体："],[465,"Mizuoto 根据文件夹里的文件识别引擎和变体，GPT-SoVITS 权重还会识别版本。识别不出时报错。"],[2,"Mizuoto 的 REST 接口、访问控制、任务、事件推送、流式合成和兼容 OpenAI 的 /v1/audio/speech，附 curl 与 Python 示例。"],[5100,"Mizuoto 的依赖及其理由、支持的平台，以及发行包怎样构建和检查：各自发布的版本、wheel、冒烟测试、CI 与发布工作流、Docker 镜像、模型镜像和本文档站。"],[5428,"Mizuoto 的开发环境只有两部分：一个 Python 环境（`.venv`），里面装着 torch、以可编辑方式安装的 Mizuoto 和开发工具；以及给 Web UI 和文档站用的 bun。所有引擎都在这一个环境里运行，不需要另外构建什么。日常任务都通过 `scripts/dev.py` 运行，它只用标准库，在 Linux、macOS 和 Windows 上行为一致，跑的正是 CI 跑的那些工具。"],[304,"Mizuoto 的模型 id；或 `tts.model_aliases` 中的别名；都不是时用 `tts.default_model`；仍没有则返回 404"],[6797,"Mizuoto 的每个引擎都是一个移植版：把上游项目的模型代码，在 Mizuoto 的运行时（`mizuoto/runtime`）和共享构件（`mizuoto/nn`、`mizuoto/text`）之上重新写一遍。不内嵌任何上游代码，也没有引擎导入 transformers、onnxruntime 或上游的包。每个移植版都遵守同一个标准：在 CPU 上、以 fp32、用同一个种子运行时，它逐采样地给出被它取代的那份代码的输出。"],[3447,"Mizuoto 的每个引擎都是对上游项目的移植，必须给出与上游**相同**的结果：在 CPU 上以 fp32、相同种子运行时，音频逐采样相同（训练器则是损失、学习率和保存的权重逐字节相同）。这条规则决定了很多写法："],[5506,"Mizuoto 的测试分三层："],[5494,"Mizuoto 的测试怎样组织：核心依靠 dummy 引擎在几秒内跑通整条链路，每个引擎和训练器都在 CI 里用小型随机模型运行（也在模拟设备上流式加载运行），真实模型有契约套件，对照工具把原生引擎与参照实现逐采样比较，行为一致性分层判断，Web UI 用 vitest，CI 覆盖三个平台和四个 Python 版本。"],[3085,"Mizuoto 的目录布局与模块边界、由测试守住的分层规则、服务的组装、一个合成请求的路径、通往模型代码的入口、引擎注册表、模型与音色、远程主机、数据目录与兼容性，以及贯穿各层的设置、事件、任务和错误。"],[585,"Mizuoto 的网页界面、命令行和 HTTP 接口都建立在同一个核心（`mizuoto.core`）之上。Python 程序可以直接使用这个核心，也可以在进程里启动一个完整的 Mizuoto 服务器。"],[2133,"Mizuoto 的设置保存在 settings.toml 中，网页界面的设置页、mizuoto config 命令和 MIZUOTO_ 环境变量改的是同一份设置；本页列出全部设置项、环境变量和数据文件夹的结构。"],[3483,"Mizuoto 的设计从哪里来：骨架的谱系，从 InvokeAI、ani2xcur、Material Design 3 和 ComfyUI 取了什么、没取什么，以及一张写明理由的设计决策表。"],[1058,"Mizuoto 目录中没有 int8 版本（官方没有公开该仓库）。"],[1191,"Mizuoto 能找到哪些 GPU"],[1097,"Mizuoto 自己使用的内部引擎：Whisper large-v3-turbo，由 Mizuoto 自己实现，约 100 种语言，为没有文本的参考音频、音色和数据集生成文本。它不出现在合成的模型列表里，也不出现在 `GET /v1/models` 中。"],[6153,"Mizuoto 自己的语音识别：Whisper large-v3-turbo（openai/whisper；权重 MIT），用于转写参考音频和音色、准备数据集，以及计算契约套件的词错误率。代码：`mizuoto/engines/asr`。它不作为合成模型提供。它完全复现 Mizuoto 0.1 运行的东西，即 transformers 4.57.3 的 `pipeline(\"automatic-speech-recognition\")`，给出与 0.1 逐 token 相同的转写结果，在 CPU 上用时约为一半。面向用户的说明见引擎详解。"],[3723,"Mizuoto 里的一个引擎由放在两处的两样东西组成，外加它的测试："],[8486,"mizuoto-model is a mirror repository holding the files Mizuoto downloads, laid out as Mizuoto keeps them:"],[469,"mizuoto-model 是一个镜像仓库，按 Mizuoto 保存的方式存放它下载的文件："],[402,"mizuoto-model 镜像"],[13117,"Mizuoto's dependencies and why, the platforms it supports, and how its distributions are made and checked: versions released on their own, wheels, the smoke test, CI and the release workflow, the Docker image, the model mirror and this docs site."],[11102,"Mizuoto's layout and module boundaries, the layer rules its tests enforce, how the services are built, the path of one synthesis request, the door to model code, the engine registry, models and voices, remote hosts, the data folder and compatibility, and the settings, events, jobs and errors every layer shares."],[14170,"Mizuoto's own speech recognition: Whisper large-v3-turbo (openai/whisper; weights MIT), used for the transcripts of reference clips and voices, for dataset preparation and for the contract suite's word error rate. Code: `mizuoto/engines/asr`. It is not offered for synthesis. It reproduces exactly what Mizuoto 0.1 ran, transformers 4.57.3's `pipeline(\"automatic-speech-recognition\")`, and gives 0.1's transcripts token for token, in about half the time on a CPU. User-facing details: Engines in depth."],[8019,"Mizuoto's REST API, access control, jobs, events, streaming synthesis and the OpenAI-compatible /v1/audio/speech, with curl and Python examples."],[11851,"Mizuoto's standard for a port is identical output to the upstream implementation on the CPU in fp32 under a seed. For the engines Mizuoto 0.1 had, `scripts/parity/` runs the same cases through 0.1's stack and the native one and compares them sample for sample (see Testing). Record what the port reproduces, where it departs and the parity result on its page in the engine reference (`site/content/docs/engines-<id>.mdx` and `.en.mdx`), and any rule a later change must not break in `AGENTS.md`."],[13523,"Mizuoto's tests come in three layers:"],[8602,"Mizuoto's web UI, command line and HTTP API are built on one core (`mizuoto.core`). A Python program can use that core directly, or start a whole Mizuoto server inside its own process."],[8358,"Mizuoto's wheel, built by `scripts/build_wheels.py`, the Fish Speech and IndexTTS wheels with `GATED=1`, and a pyopenjtalk wheel compiled for GPT-SoVITS's Japanese front end"],[11944,"Mode (`compute.vram_mode`, `engines.<id>.vram_mode`)"],[8866,"Model"],[8902,"Model"],[8956,"Model"],[8981,"Model"],[9015,"Model"],[9032,"Model"],[9060,"Model"],[9077,"Model"],[9115,"Model"],[11772,"Model"],[12353,"Model"],[12854,"Model"],[15385,"Model"],[11314,"Model and asset downloads"],[8411,"Model downloads and mirrors"],[9184,"Model downloads read the standard proxy variables `HTTPS_PROXY`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY`. Set them where `mizuoto webui` is started."],[15770,"Model downloads, engines and shared files"],[8481,"Model files you already have (an earlier download, another program's copy, your own fine-tune) can be imported instead of downloaded:"],[11290,"Model folders and the catalogue's file manifests, voices (folders, references, weights), outputs, datasets, experiments, projects and presets stay valid as they are. Only the files a manifest lists are verified, so old files a manifest dropped do no harm."],[11734,"Model handles"],[13283,"Model handles and the model manager"],[9594,"Model id, e.g. `qwen3tts/1.7b-base` (default: `tts.default_model`)"],[11279,"Model states and engine availability are the agent's (reports cached 15 s); training refuses a remote engine."],[9365,"model, device, voice, style, language, parameters, engine options and reference clips are all the same."],[4502,"model+vae 1.02"],[12519,"model+vae 1.02"],[56,"models"],[8073,"models"],[8758,"Models"],[13416,"Models"],[15020,"Models"],[15022,"Models"],[15821,"Models"],[15823,"Models"],[15834,"Models"],[11727,"Models and files manifests"],[9548,"Models and shared assets"],[10251,"Models and shared assets"],[15032,"Models are grouped by engine: speech engines first, then helpers such as speech recognition, the dummy engine last. When an engine is not available, its group says what it needs: *engine* **needs** *torch* **to use these models (mizuoto doctor).**"],[15414,"Models get their voice in different ways; **Voice** offers the ones the model supports:"],[10299,"Models kept loaded at once across every engine (1–32); the least recently used idle one is unloaded first"],[15287,"Models kept loaded at once, across all engines; beyond it the least recently used idle one is unloaded first"],[9242,"models kept loaded at once, across every engine; beyond it the least recently used idle one is unloaded first. UI: **Settings** › **Compute** › **Models kept in memory**"],[10494,"Models never unloaded for being idle or to make room for another; they give up GPU memory last"],[9251,"models never unloaded, neither for being idle nor to make room for another; they give up GPU memory last"],[14156,"Models that cross the API boundary derive from `Record` in `mizuoto/core/record.py` (pydantic v2, `json_schema_serialization_defaults_required`)."],[11076,"Models used both as a request body and in a response (`SpeakRequest`, returned by an output's re-run; a project's `Chapter`, `Line`, `Speaker`; `CommonParams`, `VoiceInput`, `EmotionInput`, `OutputSpec`…) appear twice in the schema, as `-Input` and `-Output`. The UI sends `S['SpeakRequest-Input']` and reads `S['SpeakRequest-Output']`; `webui/src/api/types.ts` aliases the common ones."],[8444,"Models with a ModelScope repository: every Qwen3-TTS, CosyVoice and VoxCPM model, and OmniVoice. CosyVoice's shared file `cosyvoice/wetext` exists on ModelScope only, so it comes from there whatever the source. The others (F5-TTS, GPT-SoVITS, IndexTTS, Fish Speech, the Whisper speech recognition model) and their shared files come from Hugging Face and compatible addresses only. On ModelScope the `master` branch is used (`cosyvoice/wetext` is pinned to a com