r(name, strict)`: one per value, so models share resolutions) and reported as `LoadedModelInfo.attention`. `LocalHandle` binds it for each step of a request with `RequestContext.accel` (the context variable lives in `runtime/context.py`, so binding loads no torch), so a stream suspended between steps never leaks its policy to another thread."],[10590,"Output and `--json`"],[71,"outputs"],[8088,"outputs"],[9566,"Outputs and jobs"],[9397,"Outputs, history, jobs and their logs"],[13638,"Over ≥ 20 texts × 3 voices × 3 seeds per voice per voice mode and model: mean CER/WER (Whisper large-v3-turbo) ≤ reference + 0.5 pp, and no case worse than the reference's worst + 5 pp; speaker similarity (CAM++ cosine to the reference clip) mean ≥ reference − 0.01; duration ratio within ±5 %; UTMOS mean ≥ reference − 0.05; loudness and F0 median within the reference's interquartile range, per voice. Failed clips (error rate above 50 %) are compared on their own (Fisher's exact test) and left out of the other measures; a threshold exceeded fails only when the paired difference is significant (Wilcoxon, p \\< 0.05)"],[10200,"Override one setting, e.g. `MIZUOTO_SERVER__PORT=8000` or `MIZUOTO_DOWNLOADS__SOURCE=hf-mirror`"],[10502,"Overrides `compute.attention` for this engine's models"],[10490,"Overrides `compute.unload_after_minutes` for this engine"],[10498,"Overrides `compute.vram_mode` for this engine's models (`auto`: the global one)"],[9248,"overrides the above for one engine"],[9519,"Overview"],[10586,"Overview"],[13133,"Packages"],[13149,"Packages"],[13453,"Packages"],[10323,"Page-locked RAM for the host copies of weights, streamed or kept for a reload (MB; 0: automatic)"],[9287,"page-locked RAM for the host copies of weights, those that stream to a GPU and those kept to reload a model (faster copies; `0`: up to 40 % of RAM on Windows, more on Linux)"],[12974,"Pageable"],[14118,"Pages"],[13274,"Pages are in `site/content/docs/`: `<slug>.mdx` in Simplified Chinese (the default language, `zh-CN`) and `<slug>.en.mdx` in English, with the same structure. The sidebars are `meta.json` and `meta.en.json`, grouped by `---Title---` separators."],[8303,"Parameter"],[8093,"Parameter presets"],[8647,"Parameter presets"],[11205,"Parameter presets"],[9923,"Parameter presets: a named set of parameters for one model, or common parameters only when no model is named."],[14729,"Parameters"],[15393,"Parameters"],[14086,"Parameters and engine options are a model's own: a new model starts from its defaults or its default preset. \"Run again\" sets them for the new model in the same watcher that resets them."],[8332,"Parameters are lenient here: one the model does not take is dropped rather than refused. Errors take OpenAI's shape, `{\"error\": {\"message\", \"type\", \"param\", \"code\"}}`, with Mizuoto's error code as `code`. A successful answer carries `X-Mizuoto-Job` and `X-Mizuoto-Model` headers."],[11726,"Parameters, options and load options"],[14168,"Parity"],[14211,"Parity"],[14313,"Parity"],[14369,"Parity"],[14419,"Parity"],[14511,"Parity"],[14588,"Parity"],[14648,"Parity"],[14724,"Parity"],[13518,"Parity with the references"],[11551,"Parsing `/openapi.json` at run time into node templates"],[11741,"Part"],[11900,"Part"],[13295,"Part"],[12082,"Partly loaded models"],[9314,"Partly loaded models run their layers' weights through RAM each time they run: a language model pays it for every generated frame, so the more of it fits, the faster it goes. Copies overlap the computation on NVIDIA and AMD GPUs; on Intel GPUs they are synchronous."],[11998,"partly loaded ones (already slow; ComfyUI's first key);"],[12607,"Partly loaded, 2 side streams"],[12002,"Partly loading a phase's components: the smaller ones load whole first, each leaving the others at least their minimum, and the largest gets what is left, its remaining units streaming."],[11949,"partly, down to the minimum"],[11955,"partly, within that half"],[13662,"pass"],[13676,"pass"],[13683,"pass"],[13690,"pass"],[13697,"pass"],[13704,"pass"],[13711,"pass"],[13718,"pass"],[13725,"pass"],[13732,"pass"],[13739,"pass"],[13746,"pass"],[13753,"pass"],[13760,"pass"],[13767,"pass"],[13782,"pass"],[13791,"pass"],[13798,"pass"],[13805,"pass"],[13812,"pass"],[13819,"pass"],[13616,"Pass"],[13788,"pass (7 % faster a request)"],[13826,"pass (GPT-SoVITS's worst clip within noise)"],[13669,"pass (worst clip within noise)"],[14874,"Passes when"],[8270,"Payload"],[13601,"Peak device memory and RAM per case, load and offload times (see Memory management)"],[12415,"Peak MB"],[12546,"Peak MB"],[12521,"Peak MB is the request's peak allocation, every model loaded in the process included. GPT-SoVITS's streamed case decodes the whole text before its first chunk (first audio 0.95 s of 0.96 s); VoxCPM's streams by patch (0.14 s)."],[10143,"PEM certificate: serve HTTPS"],[9427,"PEM certificate: serve TLS"],[10082,"PEM certificate: serve TLS (default from settings: `remote.agent.ssl_certfile`)"],[2126,"PEM 证书：以 HTTPS 提供服务"],[1410,"PEM 证书：以 TLS 提供服务"],[2065,"PEM 证书：使用 TLS（默认取自设置 `remote.agent.ssl_certfile`）"],[2221,"PEM 证书（链）：以 HTTPS 提供服务。其他电脑上的浏览器只在 HTTPS 下允许页面录音"],[14533,"Per text segment, IndexTTS-2:"],[9205,"Performance"],[12059,"Performance record"],[11884,"Phases"],[12112,"Phases (s)"],[13350,"Phases, the budget and VRAM modes, units and streaming, host copies, eviction, the exact retry, working-memory estimates and their calibration, and how an engine takes part: Memory."],[12414,"Phases, warm (s)"],[14490,"Phases: BERT around each text front-end call, HuBERT with SoVITS for the reference's semantic codes, the speaker-verification model (v2Pro), the GPT, then SoVITS (and the v4/v5 vocoder). The GPT is placed whole (its blocks read their fused projections directly; it is small, about 150 MB). A voice's own weights are switched in with `ModelHandle.replace`. The GPT's working memory is sized by the batch's longest row (its phones, the reference's codes and 16 codes a phone, within upstream's 1500 steps). With `compute.oom_fallback`, a batch that runs out of memory is spoken one text at a time."],[14397,"Phases: the codec encodes references and decodes each batch of frames; the language model (`kind=\"sequence\"`, the fast transformer `hot`) generates each batch, placed again as generation resumes. Each batch's working memory is the slow model's cache for its true bound: the references' codes, every text token, the frames of the batches before it and `max_new_tokens`, within `max_seq_len`. The model needs about 22 GB of GPU memory to run whole; with less, the runtime streams part of its weights."],[14284,"Phases: the frontend (speech tokenizer and CAM++) only for a voice that is not cached and for conversion; the language model (`kind=\"sequence\"`) makes the tokens; the flow and HiFT speak them. Streaming holds the language model and the flow together. HiFT's F0 predictor is marked `fixed` (HiFT reads its device). The language model's working memory is its cache for upstream's bound (20 speech tokens a text token after a 300-position prompt), at the KV width the model has (Qwen2's two KV heads), with one layer's copy repeated per head group, plus 512 MB. `compute.kv_cache = static` gives the Qwen2 model preallocated caches (identical on the CPU)."],[14784,"Phases: the VAE encodes a voice prompt and decodes; the model (`kind=\"sequence\"`; the local encoder and DiT `hot`, since they run many times a patch) generates; streaming holds both. If the VAE runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 latent frames."],[14571,"Phases: w2v-BERT, CAM++, the semantic codec and the regulator for a voice that is not cached (or w2v-BERT for an emotion clip); the emotion model for an emotion text; the GPT (`kind=\"sequence\"`; its GPT-2 `Conv1D` layers stream like linear layers); the s2mel; BigVGAN. A clone of a cached voice never places w2v-BERT or CAM++. If BigVGAN runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles (IndexTTS 2/2.5). The GPT's working memory is sized by each segment: its text tokens and 24 codes a token (speech runs at about 5), within `max_mel_tokens`, for every beam, in the dtype it computes in."],[9171,"pick a smaller model (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, for one)."],[13484,"Pin the catalogue models' files (sizes, SHA-256) (`scripts/model_manifests.py`)"],[12975,"Pinned in place"],[8599,"Pinned settings"],[8710,"Pinned settings, shaped like `settings.toml`"],[8618,"Pinned settings, shaped like `settings.toml`; never written to the file"],[15572,"Plain audio files"],[15395,"Plan, Speak and Stream"],[11707,"Planning should not wait on a model, but the result must be usable"],[11211,"Planning, `speak` / `convert` / `edit` jobs, streaming"],[13192,"Platforms"],[10686,"Policies"],[9419,"Port"],[10078,"Port (default from settings: `7870`)"],[11504,"Port selection"],[14604,"Post-processing without pydub (`Segment`: pydub's millisecond arithmetic on int16 arrays, `audioop.rms`)"],[14748,"Precision: `auto` is upstream's choice, the config's bf16 on every device including the CPU, float32 on Apple MPS; `engines.voxcpm.dtype` overrides. The VAE always runs in float32."],[10482,"Precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`"],[9232,"precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`. UI: **Precision** on the engine's card"],[14173,"Precision: bf16 on a CUDA GPU that has it (else fp16), fp32 elsewhere; `engines.asr.dtype` overrides."],[14593,"Precision: bf16 on a CUDA GPU that has it (else fp16), fp32 elsewhere; `engines.omnivoice.dtype` overrides."],[14667,"Precision: bf16 on a CUDA GPU that has it (else fp16), fp32 elsewhere; `engines.qwen3tts.dtype` overrides."],[14373,"Precision: bf16 on a CUDA GPU, as upstream; fp32 elsewhere (bf16 is emulated on a CPU and far slower); `engines.fishspeech.dtype` overrides."],[14329,"Precision: fp16 on a CUDA GPU of compute capability 7 or more, as upstream's `load_checkpoint` decides; fp32 elsewhere."],[14448,"Precision: fp16 on a CUDA GPU when `engines.gpts