ket)"],[13288,"Streams are generators"],[11565,"Strict mode (`server.strict_port`, `--strict-port`) fails instead of moving on, for reverse proxies and containers with fixed port mappings."],[10688,"Structured masks"],[10828,"structured: causal, keys padded on one side, a window"],[15392,"Style"],[14045,"Styles use tokens only: the colour roles `--md-sys-color-*` (generated from the seed colour by `applyTheme.ts`), spacing `--app-space-*`, in-page stacking `--app-z-*`, type classes such as `type-title-large`."],[10622,"Success"],[10941,"Suppression and EOS masks are built once per device; `repetition_penalty_seen` applies the penalty over a mask of the drawn ids, so shapes do not grow."],[12748,"Switch"],[13907,"Switch a method off and say why"],[16008,"Switch to a real engine"],[10693,"Sync-free sampling"],[10703,"Sync-free sampling"],[10367,"Synthesis jobs (speak, voice conversion, speech editing) that may run at once across every engine and device (1–16); the others wait in the queue in order. Requests run together as one micro-batch count as one job"],[9257,"synthesis jobs (speak, voice conversion, speech editing) that may run at once across every engine and device; requests run together as one micro-batch (`tts.micro_batch`) count as one. UI: **Synthesis jobs at once**"],[15293,"Synthesis jobs (speak, voice conversion, speech editing) that run at once, across every engine and device; more wait in the queue in order, showing **Waiting for other synthesis jobs**. Requests run together as one batch (**Run waiting requests together**) count as one job"],[9258,"Synthesis jobs run `compute.inference_jobs` at a time (one by default), whatever engine and device they use; the others wait in the queue in order (**Waiting for other synthesis jobs**). `compute.gpu_jobs` still limits the jobs on each GPU."],[8087,"Synthesis, conversion, editing, what a model takes"],[8653,"Synthesis: `plan`, `speak`, `convert`, `edit`"],[10259,"Synthesized audio"],[15987,"Synthesized results"],[9138,"System"],[10174,"System"],[15967,"System"],[14875,"T0 operation"],[6858,"T0 操作"],[14878,"T1 module"],[6861,"T1 模块"],[14881,"T2 stage"],[6864,"T2 阶段"],[2916,"T2S 的单 token 步骤围绕每层的注意力，每种行数一组；采样即时执行"],[14884,"T3 end to end"],[6867,"T3 端到端"],[13520,"T4 results"],[5503,"T4 结果"],[11771,"Table"],[13208,"Tag"],[8530,"Take verified copies from here; can be given more than once"],[15094,"Takes"],[15200,"Takes are FLAC results and are not listed in History. Deleting a line, a chapter or the project deletes their takes."],[12428,"talker 0.76, codec decoder 0.03"],[4411,"talker 0.76、codec decoder 0.03"],[12421,"talker 1.22, codec decoder 0.05"],[4404,"talker 1.22、codec decoder 0.05"],[12120,"talker 19.9, codec decoder 0.9"],[4103,"talker 19.9，codec decoder 0.9"],[12116,"talker 30.2, codec decoder 4.0"],[4099,"talker 30.2，codec decoder 4.0"],[6661,"talker 和 code predictor，基于 `runtime/lm/qwen.py`"],[6680,"talker 的工作内存按请求估算：每行的提示（指令、参考文本和编码、文本）加上每个文本 token 16 帧（实际语音约 3–4 帧），不超过 `max_new_tokens`，缓存峰值按比其大小多一层计，再加 256 MB。所以在 1.7B 模型上一句话只预留约 300–400 MB，而不是按最坏情况（8192 帧）要求的数 GB，显存紧张时 talker 也不会被无谓地流式加载。`compute.kv_cache = static` 为 talker 和 code predictor 提供预分配的缓存（CPU 上结果相同）。"],[13469,"Task"],[11733,"Task types"],[13313,"Task types"],[7520,"Teach it a speaker"],[15537,"Teach it a speaker"],[13628,"Teacher-forced logits; discrete outputs from captured inputs (speech-tokenizer codes, VQ codes, ODE trajectories with injected noise)"],[14882,"teacher-forced logits; discrete outputs from captured inputs (speech-tokenizer codes, VQ codes)"],[10880,"TensorFloat-32 matrix products and cuDNN convolutions (NVIDIA, Ampere on)"],[2863,"TensorFloat-32 矩阵乘法和 cuDNN 卷积（NVIDIA，Ampere 及以后）"],[13562,"Test"],[14049,"Test"],[13510,"Testing"],[11750,"Tests"],[11434,"Tests a change needs"],[11236,"Tests build fully isolated services with `environ=` (instead of `os.environ`), `data_dir=` and `settings_overrides=` (`make_services` in `tests/conftest.py`). The dummy engine runs in the test's own process, as every engine does."],[13548,"Tests that need the scheduler and the reaper pass `start_background=True`. The API tests do: `create_app(make_services(start_background=True), bound_host=\"127.0.0.1\", serve_ui=False)`, then `TestClient`."],[11879,"Tests: `tests/engines_native/test_<id>_tiny.py` (an engine in its own distribution keeps them in its package's `tests/`, as `packages/native/<pkg>/tests/` do); the engine id list in `tests/core/test_engines.py::test_registry_lookups` and the `engines` override in `tests/engines/test_contract.py`."],[13144,"Text"],[15391,"Text"],[9716,"Text to look for in names, descriptions and tags (`list`)"],[14749,"Text tokens and audio patches share one sequence. Per patch, a **text-semantic language model** (MiniCPM-4 with LongRoPE and a static KV cache) and a shallower **residual acoustic language model** produce two hidden states; a **local DiT** (a bidirectional MiniCPM-4 run as a conditional flow, about 10 Euler steps with classifier-free guidance) predicts the next patch of latents from them and the previous patch; a **local encoder** embeds the patch back into the language model; a **stop head** decides whether to continue. The **AudioVAE**, a DAC-like causal convolutional codec with Snake activations, decodes the latents (v2 with sample-rate conditioning, 16 kHz latents to 48 kHz audio)."],[13544,"That is how cancellation at the next check, OOM becoming `compute_unavailable`, timeouts, unloading, the reaper and streamed chunks are all checked in seconds on a CI machine without a GPU. The dummy engine is also how users try Mizuoto out, and `smoke_wheels.py` uses it."],[11655,"That is the weights' licence; the non-commercial term is conveyed by tags and a notice"],[13837,"that package's `gated` and `oldest-mizuoto` jobs, and `torch` for it"],[10207,"The \"UI\" column names the place in the web UI's **Settings**; engine settings are on the engine's card in **Models** › **Engines**."],[15562,"The **Add clips** part of a dataset's page offers several sources:"],[15201,"The **Export** tab:"],[15731,"the **Main clip** badge, or **Make it the main clip**. The main clip comes first when the voice is cloned, and is the one played from the list."],[16027,"The **Speak** button at the bottom is replaced by the one step the model still needs, here **Download Qwen3-TTS 1.7B CustomVoice (size)**. Click it and wait for the progress bar. (When torch is missing, it shows the command that installs it instead.)"],[15438,"The **Text** box takes up to 20,000 characters. Ctrl+Enter in it speaks."],[14047,"The `/dev` route (`DevComponentsView.vue`) shows every `ui/` component, for checking them by eye."],[13242,"The `Dockerfile` at the repository root builds one image: the server, its web UI and every engine, with GPT-SoVITS's Japanese and Korean front ends (and IndexTTS-2.5's Japanese with `GATED=1`). Models go into the `/data` volume."],[8349,"The `Dockerfile` at the repository's root builds one image with the Mizuoto server, its web UI and every engine, torch included; models download into the data volume."],[13989,"The `export` stage returns `{\"artifacts\": [...]}`, which the host's `_register` takes in:"],[10204,"The `MIZUOTO_` prefix is dropped and the rest lower-cased; `__` (two underscores) goes one level down: `MIZUOTO_COMPUTE__GPU_JOBS` is `compute.gpu_jobs`, `MIZUOTO_ENGINES__QWEN3TTS__DEVICE` is `engines.qwen3tts.device`, `MIZUOTO_REMOTE__AGENT__PORT` is `remote.agent.port`."],[10604,"The `mizuoto` command line does what the web UI does: speak, clone and design voices, convert and edit recordings, transcribe, check torch and the engines, manage models, presets, projects, datasets and training, remote hosts, jobs and settings. It is a thin wrapper: each command parses its arguments, calls the **one** core method for that operation and prints the result. The HTTP API behind the web UI calls the same methods, so both behave alike, and the records `--json` prints have the same shape as the API's JSON."],[13337,"The `ModelManager` (`manager.py`, ComfyUI's `load_models_gpu` / `free_memory`) keeps every registered handle with its owner (`<model id>@<device>`) and last use, and places handles **whole or partly** for each phase of a request (`ctx.use`, `ctx.run`): idle components give up memory unit by unit, a model that does not fit keeps part of its weights in RAM and streams them to the device as its layers run, and a phase that runs out of memory runs again, exactly, with more weights streamed. The policy (`policy.py`, `VramPolicy`) comes from the `compute` settings at each load."],[11229,"The `open_services()` context manager (the CLI's through `cli/output.py`), built once per command and closed after"],[10184,"The `paths.*` settings move models, voices, outputs, datasets, experiments, projects and caches elsewhere one by one; empty means inside the data folder, and so does a relative folder (`results` is `<data folder>/results`, whatever folder Mizuoto is started from)."],[13248,"The `python:<version>-slim` base of the wheels stage and the image"],[14006,"The `ui/` wrapper layer"],[8309,"The `X-Mizuoto-Sample-Rate` header is the rate and `X-Mizuoto-Job` the job (the result is still stored). Streaming text is not available this way."],[14553,"The 1.5/2 front end: WeTextProcessing's FSTs through kaldifst (`TnProcessor`), `TextNormalizer`, SentencePiece, `split_segments`"],[14682,"The 12 Hz speech tokenizer: a Mimi-style encoder (transformers' `MimiModel` encode path) and a causal decoder (72-frame attention window, SnakeBeta upsampling)"],[14555,"The 2.5 front end: punctuation map, normalisation, fugashi for Japanese, tiktoken with `<\\|lang\\|>`"],[14384,"The 44.1 kHz codec"],[9103,"the above plus **Emotion from a clip**, **Emotion sliders**, **Emotion from text**, **Streaming**"],[8937,"the above plus **Preset speakers** (no inline tags)"],[10566,"The address this machine listens on as an agent; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[8689,"The address to bind"],[15272,"The address to listen on (`127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only) and the port (7869 by default). **Takes effect the next time the server starts.**"],[15958,"The address to listen on, `127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only"],[9520,"The advanced section is for readers who already use Mizuoto and want to know more about the engines, the API, remote hosts, performance, downloads, containers and calling it from Python."],[13428,"The agent answers each operation with `progress`, `chunk` (a binary frame: float32 little-endian mono) and `file` frames, then a `result` or `error`, and beats every 5 s. With no frame for `remote.heartbeat_timeout` (60 s), the host closes the session with `worker_failed` (`during = \"heartbeat\"`); the next request reconnects."],[9503,"The agent beats every 5 s while it works; a request whose agent stays silent this long fails"],[9470,"The agent cannot be reached"],[8409,"The agent has its own volume and models; build its image like the host's (same Mizuoto version, `GATED=1` if it serves the gated engines). The image's health check asks the web UI's port 7869, which an agent does not serve, hence `--no-healthcheck`. Without TLS, requests and audio cross the network unencrypted: use a trusted network, or give a certificate with `--ssl-certfile` / `--ssl-keyfile` (mount the files into the container)."],[9436,"The agent runs in the foreground until Ctrl+C. Its idle unloading and GPU memory handling follow that machine's settings (`compute.*`, `engines.<id>.*`). A port in use stops it with a hint to choose another `--port`."],[9447,"The agent serves TLS"],[9432,"The agent uses that machine's own data folder (settings, models, cache), as `mizuoto webui` there would; set `MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR` to give it another one. It runs the engines in its own process."],[9381,"The agent: the machine with the engines"],[10554,"The agent's `host:port` (port 7870 by default)"],[9443,"The agent's `host` or `host:port` (port 7870 by default); IPv6 as `[::1]:7870`"],[10569,"The agent's port"],[10575,"The agent's TLS certificate"],[10557,"The agent's token (`remote.agent.token` on that machine)"],[9445,"The agent's token. Left out when changing a host, the saved one is kept"],[10972,"The API (`mizuoto/api/`) and the command line (`mizuoto/cli/`) are two thin shells over one core: parse the input, call one core method, shape the output. This page covers both shells and their conventions; the core itself is in Architecture, and how the web UI consumes these endpoints is in Web UI."],[13490,"The API server (7869) and the Vite dev server (5173) together; Ctrl+C stops both"],[11569,"The app is built inside a function, not at import time, so each test gets a fresh one; `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py` compares the whole command tree, so a forgotten registration fails."],[10961,"The app: `create_app()`"],[12005,"the attempt's exception frame is left first (it holds the failed attempt's tensors);"],[12066,"The attention dispatcher"],[11680,"The attention policy is bound per request step for inference, and process-wide for a training stage"],[10768,"The attentions that add relative positions inside the scores, or need the probability matrix, are not sites: wenet's relative attention, IndexTTS's Conformer, w2v-BERT, VITS, plus the s3tokenizer (q and k each scaled by d^-¼), MelStyle and G2PW's BERT. They stay hand-written, since no fused kernel computes them. `Site(swappable=False)` keeps a site on its reference whatever the policy; `approx_ok=False` refuses every backend that is not exact."],[14594,"The audio is 8 codebooks of the HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer. The language model, Qwen3-0.6B run **bidirectionally**, sees the style tokens, the text, the reference's codes and the target as masked positions; over a fixed number of steps (32 by default) it unmasks the most confident codes, with classifier-free guidance in log-probability space, a per-codebook penalty and Gumbel noise on positions. Every step is a full forward over the whole sequence (no KV cache). The target length comes from a rule-based estimate (per-script character weights scaled by the reference's speaking rate), or from `speed` and `duration`."],[14177,"The audio is cut into 30 s windows overlapping by 5 s on each side, each window's features computed as `WhisperFeatureExtractor` computes them, four windows per `generate` call."],[10779,"the backends with a backward pass (not `sage`, `sage3`)"],[8240,"The body is a `SpeakRequest`. Its main fields (`/docs` has all of them):"],[8266,"The body of `PUT /api/v1/audio/files` is the file itself (not multipart); the `name` query parameter names it. The `id` it returns is a reference's `audio_id`:"],[11498,"The body says why, the measured or compared results, and any behaviour deliberately kept."],[11564,"The bound socket is handed to uvicorn (`server.run(sockets=[sock])`): there is no gap between checking and serving."],[14138,"The boundary that decides where code goes is now inside the package: **`mizuoto/core` never imports torch at module level**, and `mizuoto/core/inference` is its only door to model code (`mizuoto.runtime`, `mizuoto.nn`, `mizuoto.engines`, `mizuoto.training`), always imported inside functions. So `mizuoto version`, `mizuoto --help` and the core's own tests load no torch, and a command that never loads a model never imports the runtime. Architecture starts from that rule."],[11885,"The budget"],[11560,"The build uses `base: './'`, and at run time `api/baseUrl.ts` derives the deployment root from the entry script's URL (everything before the last `/assets/`); routes use hash history. One build works at the root and under an `--api-prefix` sub-path with no rewriting."],[13362,"The building blocks engines share live beside the runtime: `mizuoto/nn` (DSP bit-exact with torchaudio, librosa and Whisper; flows; transformers; vocoders; codecs; SSL and speaker encoders) and `mizuoto/text` (BPE tokenizers identical to transformers' for the models Mizuoto runs, Whisper's vocabulary, wetext's normaliser)."],[13467,"The built `dist/` ships in the wheel as package data; `mizuoto webui` from a checkout without `dist/` serves the API but no UI."],[10168,"the built-in defaults;"],[10862,"the call needs a backward pass or dropout it lacks;"],[13404,"The caller passes an `EngineRequest` with its `cancel` event (a job's `cancel_event`), an optional `timeout`, the streamed-text queue (`text_input`, filled by `TextFeed`) and a `progress` callback. A small watcher thread checks every 20 ms: it copies the caller's cancel into the context's cancel event, and past the timeout it marks the call timed out and cancels it. The engine stops at its next `check_cancel()`; the call then fails with `CancelledError`, or `OperationTimeoutError` after a timeout. When the call ends, the handle copies `applied`, `warnings` and `timings[\"total\"]` into the `EngineRequest`."],[15244,"The cast and each line's state (with chapter and line ids)"],[9950,"The cast and every line with its state"],[11640,"The catalogue downloads only files the engines read"],[9075,"The catalogue has no int8 version: no public repository exists for it."],[9431,"The certificate's private key"],[10084,"The certificate's private key"],[10146,"The certificate's private key"],[10578,"The certificate's private key"],[10242,"The certificate's private key, when the certificate file lacks it"],[9328,"the CFM estimator"],[10895,"the CFM estimator (each SoVITS model loaded, a voice's own too)"],[8294,"The client sends one JSON text message: a `SpeakRequest`."],[14610,"The closed design vocabulary and `_resolve_instruct`"],[12584,"The code and settings proven only on the CPU, checked on the free GPUs of the GPU baseline (2026-10-18)."],[11531,"The code as it is"],[13204,"The code has paths for these devices (device probing, float64 modules on the CPU where a device lacks float64, no compilation on MPS, CUDA graphs and half precision only on CUDA) and they are tested on simulated devices, but they have not been verified on AMD, Intel or Apple hardware."],[11049,"The code strings live in `mizuoto/core/codes.py` (standard library only), so engines and training stages raise them without pydantic; `error_from_code()` rebuilds the class from a code."],[10970,"The command line"],[15502,"The command line (`--span` is repeatable, `START:END[:SECONDS]` in seconds):"],[10664,"The command line and a server can open the same data folder at the same time. They are separate processes sharing the settings file, the database and the folders:"],[11226,"The command line and Python"],[15056,"The command line can name it, or move rather than copy: `mizuoto model import <folder> [--name name] [--move]`."],[11567,"The command line follows ani2xcur's Typer layout:"],[8345,"The command line in the container"],[14975,"The command line:"],[14980,"The command line:"],[15490,"The command line:"],[11505,"The command line: Typer registration"],[8396,"The command: `mizuoto webui --host 0.0.0.0 --port 7869 --no-open`."],[10588,"The commands"],[14005,"The component layer: `src/ui/`"],[14036,"The components `@material/web` has are wrapped in project Vue components: buttons (`AppButton`: filled, tonal, outlined, text), icon buttons, FAB, checkbox, filter chip, divider, text field and text area, slider, linear and circular progress, switch, tabs. The wrapper owns the props, the event names and the types; `vite.config.ts` declares `md-*` tags as custom elements."],[14807,"The conditions"],[9491,"The connection drops or the agent stops answering"],[13482,"The contract suite against the installed models (`MIZUOTO_TEST_DEVICE=cpu\\|cuda:N`)"],[14797,"The contract suite passes (18 tests across the three models)."],[14300,"The contract suite passes (18 tests)."],[11428,"The conventions code in Mizuoto follows: style, the layer rules, the rules for native code, the exactness rule, the steps for adding a command, route, setting or engine option, what tests a change needs, documentation in both languages and the commit message format."],[14382,"The conversation prompt, sampling in upstream's order, turn grouping, the decoder (`Decoder`) with its CUDA graphs"],[13008,"The copies themselves now run at 13.2 GB/s (98 % of the link, measured over the talker's own host tensors); what remains of a reload is allocating the device memory again, 0.08–0.1 s for the talker, since giving memory up empties the allocator's cache (on purpose: other processes get it back). Expandable segments allocate no faster. The smaller models have more small tensors, which stay pageable (under 1 MB). Under a cap, the streamer used to copy streamed weights into page-locked memory at 1.5 GB/s on the first request; registering them in place took that off the cold request: F5-TTS 5.40 → 4.99 s, OmniVoice 5.96 → 5.07 s, CosyVoice 2/3 20.82/16.93 → 19.36/14.10 s, GPT-SoVITS v4 6.51 → 5.65 s, Fish Speech 44.89 → 41.23 s, IndexTTS 2 36.10 → 33.54 s, VoxCPM 2 29.12 → 26.85 s, Qwen3-TTS 9.22/10.90 → 8.57/9.86 s; warm requests and every output identical."],[11746,"The core (`EngineRegistry`), without importing the engine"],[11474,"The core method (`Record` in and out) → a route with an `operation_id` in `api/routers/` → `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and commit `schema.d.ts` → `tests/api/test_api.py`. See Adding a route"],[11753,"The core plans and validates every request from the manifest alone, then calls the implementation through `core/inference` (see Runtime). This page walks through OmniVoice: `mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/omnivoice.toml` and `mizuoto/engines/omnivoice/`."],[14130,"The core, the API, the command line, the web UI (its built `dist/` ships in the wheel), the runtime, the building blocks and every engine under a permissive licence"],[11488,"The core's behaviour is tested with the dummy engine (no torch, no model); the network is replaced by `httpx.MockTransport`; tests get an isolated data folder and an empty environment from `make_services`."],[11606,"The cost of running in process (a crash in native code takes the server down; no memory release by process exit) is paid for by rules"],[14297,"the CosyVoice 3 English clone: about 23 dB (CAM++'s float noise, above);"],[14203,"The CosyVoice engine as implemented in Mizuoto: CosyVoice 1, 2 and 3, speech tokenizers and CAM++ from their ONNX files, the language models, flows and HiFT, what reproduces upstream exactly and why the whole stack is not bit-identical, the GPU decoding path, the LLM and flow fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[8684,"the data folder"],[10138,"the data folder"],[8387,"The data folder"],[8680,"The data folder"],[10194,"The data folder"],[8609,"The data folder (database, models, voices, outputs, caches)"],[11114,"The data folder and compatibility"],[10152,"The data folder and the settings file"],[15019,"The data folder can be moved, renamed or copied: start Mizuoto with the new location (`MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR`, or `mizuoto webui --data-dir`) and every result plays from there. A result whose file is gone shows **File missing**; `mizuoto output check` lists such results, and `--prune-missing` removes them."],[11295,"The data folder can be moved, renamed, copied or opened through a link, and the database must follow it. `outputs.path` and `audio_files.path` therefore record a file inside the data folder relative to it (`outputs/2026-10/a.wav`, with `/` on every platform), and a file elsewhere (a server path, an outputs folder set outside the data folder) absolute. `mizuoto/core/storage.py` owns that rule (`StorageService.store` / `resolve`, over `to_stored` / `from_stored` in `core/files.py`); records handed out (`Output.path`, `AudioFile.path`) are absolute, as the file is on disk now, with `missing` set when it is gone."],[11287,"The data folder defaults to `mizuoto` in the platform's user data folder (`~/.local/share/mizuoto` on Linux, under `%APPDATA%` on Windows, under `~/Library/Application Support` on macOS); `MIZUOTO_DATA_DIR` puts it elsewhere. It holds `models/` (with 