323,"The exact path is 5 % behind qwen-tts-webui, the fused one level with it, both in 12 % less memory; the exact path's audio repeats sample for sample between rounds."],[15625,"The experiment's page shows the base model, the dataset, the result and the language. **Stages** is a row of steps, each **Not run**, **Running**, **Done**, **Out of date** or **Failed**."],[10530,"The export stage speaks a dataset clip's text with what was trained"],[14306,"The F5-TTS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: v1 Base, v0 Base and E2, the DiT and UNetT, the CFM sampler and Vocos, what reproduces upstream exactly, memory and compile notes, the full fine-tune, and its parity results."],[14304,"The fast decoding path is CUDA only."],[11284,"The file is checked for outside changes every second; every change, wherever it came from, reaches the `on_keys_change` listeners as dotted keys (`changed_keys`)."],[13833,"The first job, `scope`, reads the changed files (a push's from the compare API, a pull request's from its file list) and `python scripts/ci.py scope` maps them to checks:"],[12408,"The first measurement on a free GPU (conditions above), of commit `4e6fe35`, frozen in a worktree. Every engine ran with its GPU defaults (`dtype = auto`, CUDA graphs on), three runs per case in one process per engine, with two streamed cases added. Warm is the faster of the two later runs; the first request includes the model's load."],[13828,"The first opt-in runs exposed a harness bug: requests and the parity cases had put engine options under `options`, which the request model does not have and pydantic ignores, so `packed_guidance` and six T3 cases (GPT-SoVITS's cut5, batch and serial cases, VoxCPM's continuation and retry) had run with the defaults. They now use `engine_options`; rerun on the CPU, the six are identical to 0.1 and upstream sample for sample with their options applied."],[15952,"The first port to try, from the settings by default (7869); `0` picks any free port"],[13110,"The first request pays the compilation: +30 s to +160 s. The audio is not identical (Acceleration)."],[9334,"The first requests pay the compilation: on a CPU, 30 s to 160 s more."],[14949,"The first synthesis"],[14986,"The first synthesis loads the model into the server's process, which takes a while; then the model stays in memory until it has been idle for the time set under **Settings › Compute**. When the GPU has less free memory than the model needs, Mizuoto fails at once with **The GPU is not available or ran out of memory**, and **What to do** says how to fix it, such as another device or freeing GPU memory."],[15401,"The first time, the screen picks **Settings › Speech › Default model**, or else the first model that is ready. Then it remembers your last choice."],[14362,"The Fish Speech S2 Pro engine as implemented in Mizuoto's separate mizuoto-fishspeech distribution: the dual-AR transformer and the 44.1 kHz codec, what reproduces upstream exactly, one wait per frame and CUDA graphs, the LoRA fine-tune, and its parity results."],[9326,"the flow estimator"],[10893,"the flow estimator"],[8683,"The folder for `settings.toml` (your application's configuration folder, for instance); the data stays in `data_dir`"],[10196,"The folder for `settings.toml`, when it should not sit in the data folder"],[8612,"The folder holding `settings.toml`"],[11703,"The folders are the truth, and a scan cannot drift from the files; hundreds of voices scan in milliseconds"],[14035,"The font (`@fontsource-variable/roboto-flex`) and the icons are bundled into `dist/`: the UI loads nothing from outside and works offline."],[11653,"The former need another model and a ModelScope pipeline, and are all off in upstream's default generation; there is no public int8 repository"],[14471,"The front end: `frontend.py` (cleaner, `TextPreprocessor`), segmentation, language detection (split-lang, fast-langdetect), Chinese (tone sandhi, normalisation, G2PW), English (normalisation, tagger, g2p_en), Japanese, Korean (g2pk2), Cantonese, symbols and data"],[13275,"The frontmatter has `title`, `description` and `icon` (a Lucide icon name). The MDX components are in `site/src/components/mdx.tsx`: `Cards`/`Card`, `Callout`, `Tabs`/`Tab`, `Steps`/`Step`, `Accordions`/`Accordion` and `Mermaid` (a `chart` prop; rendered in the browser with Mermaid loaded from a CDN, following the site's light or dark theme)."],[15914,"The full development setup is in Development setup."],[11770,"The full list is `Capability` in `models.py`. Some drive the pipeline: without `long_text` Mizuoto segments the text; `batch` with `max_batch > 1` enables micro-batching; `stream_audio`'s granularity comes from `stream_granularity`; `stream_text_input` allows streamed text over the WebSocket. A variant may also have `languages`, `speakers`, `emotions`, `inline_tags`, `instruct_requires` and `weights_version`."],[14747,"The generation comes from `config.json`'s `architecture` (missing means `voxcpm`); 1.5 is the first generation with a 44.1 kHz VAE. The model folder holds `config.json`, `model.safetensors` (else `pytorch_model.bin`), `audiovae.pth` (else `audiovae.safetensors`), `tokenizer.json` and `tokenizer_config.json`. A voice's cache holds the VAE latents of the prompt (left-padded) and of the reference (right-padded), as upstream's `build_prompt_cache` makes them."],[12252,"The generator jumped ahead instead of drawing: MT19937's state after *n* draws computed in GF(2) (`mizuoto/training/rng.py`), 204 jumps in 2.3 s instead of 41–52 s"],[14491,"The GPT is small and launch-bound: a step is about 360 small kernels and used to wait for the device twice (upstream's two end-of-sequence checks), plus a Python boolean copied to the device by top-p. Now the two checks are read together (the same boolean) and the copy is a `fill_`: one wait per step. With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the GPT wholly on its device) its one-token steps run as graphs around each layer's attention, one set per number of rows (rows drop as they finish); the cache, grown by concatenation, and the sampling stay eager on the request's generator. A voice's own GPT gets its own graphs. The real v2, v2Pro and v4 models give the same audio with and without graphs, 1.3–2.0 times faster per request."],[10936,"the GPT-2's one-token steps around each layer's attention; the cache, its beam reorder and the sampling eager"],[14412,"The GPT-SoVITS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: v2, v2Pro, v2ProPlus, v4 and v5 Turbo, the text front end with its ported converters and models, the T2S model, SoVITS and the flow, what reproduces upstream exactly, GPU decoding, the speaker fine-tune that writes upstream's files, and its parity results."],[9458,"The handshake succeeded"],[11861,"The HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer: `nn/codecs/dac`, `nn/ssl/hubert`, residual codebooks"],[14988,"The History screen: every result, to search, filter by model, mark as favourite, run again, download and delete."],[13426,"The host connects and sends `hello` with the token (compared with `hmac.compare_digest`) and its protocol. An agent of another protocol refuses the host with a hint to install the same Mizuoto version on both machines, and the host refuses such an agent in turn. Otherwise the agent answers with its `AgentInfo`: version, devices, which engines are available there and its installed models."],[8739,"The host enters the child app's `lifespan` on its own event loop (it forwards events to the socket) and calls `services.close()` on the way out. `start_background=True` starts the job scheduler and the unloading of idle models; without it, queued jobs do not run. `create_app` also takes `extra_hosts` (a set; names added to it later are accepted at once) and `serve_ui=False` (the API only)."],[9452,"The host is contacted at once: online, the command prints the agent's machine name, Mizuoto version, devices and installed engines; unreachable, the host is saved anyway and its state (`offline` or `refused`) is shown."],[12051,"The 