emselves under the Python entry-point group `mizuoto.engines`."],[11561,"The UI is built before the wheel: `scripts/build_wheels.py` runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and `bun run build`, then builds the sdist and the wheel; Docker builds it in a bun stage of its own, and the final image carries no Node toolchain. See Release."],[14018,"The UI is built on Material Design 3 (M3) in two layers: a **token layer** that everything reads, and a **component layer** on top of it. The token layer depends on no component library; the component layer can be replaced piece by piece."],[16015,"The UI opens on **Speak**; nothing has to be set up before you try it. Two settings are worth a look before downloading a real model:"],[14951,"The UI opens on **Speak**. Nothing has to be set up first: the dummy engine works right away (it speaks in tones), so you can look around before downloading anything. Three places matter for a real engine:"],[15775,"The UI opens on the screen you were last on. Each screen keeps its state (and scroll position) while you visit others; the page of each voice, dataset, experiment and project keeps its own."],[11573,"The UI uses Material Design 3 in two layers:"],[15268,"The UI's language; **Auto** follows the browser"],[11899,"The user-facing settings are in Performance; the runtime as a whole in Runtime."],[11094,"The usual shape of a command (`commands/projects.py`):"],[14469,"The v4/v5 48 kHz HiFi-GAN; the ERes2NetV2 speaker-verification embedding"],[12022,"the VAE in tiles"],[8732,"The values in `settings` sit above the settings file and the environment, are **never written to the file**, and cannot be changed through the web UI or the API:"],[14666,"The variant comes from `config.json` (`tts_model_type`, `tts_model_size`); only `tokenizer_type = qwen3_tts_tokenizer_12hz` is accepted. The model folder holds `config.json`, `model.safetensors`, the tokenizer files (`tokenizer.json`, or `vocab.json` + `merges.txt` + `tokenizer_config.json`) and `speech_tokenizer/` (`config.json`, `model.safetensors`). A Base voice's cache is `prompt.pt`, the clone prompt (reference codes and speaker embedding)."],[14446,"The variant comes from the base GPT and SoVITS pair in the model folder, laid out as upstream lays it out: `gsv-v2final-pretrained/…`, `s1v3.ckpt`, `v2Pro/s2Gv2Pro.pth` / `s2Gv2ProPlus.pth`, `gsv-v4-pretrained/{s2Gv4,vocoder}.pth`, `gsv-v5-pretrained/{s2Gv5turbo,vocoder}.pth`. A voice's own weights (`Voice.weights[\"gptsovits\"]`: a GPT `.ckpt` and a SoVITS `.pth`, version read from the file) replace the base pair for that voice."],[14250,"The variant comes from the yaml in the folder (`cosyvoice.yaml`, `cosyvoice2.yaml`, `cosyvoice3.yaml`); a CosyVoice 1 folder with `spk2info.pt` is SFT or Instruct. The folder holds the yaml, `llm.pt`, `flow.pt`, `hift.pt`, `campplus.onnx`, `speech_tokenizer_v1.onnx` / `v2` / `v3`, `spk2info.pt`, and for v2/v3 the `CosyVoice-BlankEN` config and tokenizer (not its weights, which `llm.pt` replaces). The shared asset `cosyvoice/wetext` holds the text normaliser's FSTs. The ONNX models are converted once and cached as `<model>/.mizuoto/converted-<key>.safetensors` (a `<name>.safetensors` beside the ONNX file wins)."],[11803,"The variant from the folder's files only, without torch"],[10871,"the version: flash-attn ≥ 2.6; xFormers outside 0.0.21–0.0.26 (broken for large batches) and with its C++ kernels (`_has_cpp_library`: a wheel for another torch imports without them);"],[10115,"The versions of Mizuoto, Python and the main components (torch, fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, typer, httpx, numpy, av, `mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`; a component that is not installed has no version). Option: `--json`."],[8081,"The voice library"],[10255,"The voice library"],[11214,"The voice library (folders), fit, design, export/import"],[15985,"The voice library, one folder per voice"],[9395,"The voice library, reference clips and voice caches"],[8657,"The voice library: `list_voices`, `get`, `create_from_audio`"],[15688,"The voice library: make voices from audio, design them, add preset speakers, manage clips, transcripts and fine-tuned weights, see which models can use them, export and import."],[15766,"The voice library: make, design, import and export voices, and see which models can use them"],[15810,"The voice library: voices from clips (speech recognition fills in missing transcripts), designed voices, preset speakers and voices with their own fine-tuned weights; export and import."],[14252,"The voice prompt is made from the reference three times over: 16 kHz audio to a Whisper log-mel to the **speech tokenizer**'s tokens; 16 kHz audio to a kaldi fbank to **CAM++**'s 192-dim speaker embedding; and always a 24 kHz Matcha mel, even for the 22.05 kHz CosyVoice 1. The **language model** turns text (and the prompt's text and tokens) into speech tokens; the **flow** turns tokens into a mel in 10 Euler steps with guidance 0.7; **HiFT** (a HiFi-GAN with a neural source filter and an inverse STFT) turns the mel into audio."],[9654,"The voice, described"],[9752,"The voice, described"],[15185,"The voice: **Library voice**, **Preset speaker** or **Its own voice**, as the model supports. The library picker shows how this model can use each voice, as in Speak."],[15530,"the voice's GPT and SoVITS weights"],[9733,"The voice's language"],[9727,"The voice's name"],[9748,"The voice's name"],[15691,"The voice's page"],[14717,"The VoxCPM engine as implemented in Mizuoto: VoxCPM2, 1.5 and 0.5B, MiniCPM-4, the local DiT and the AudioVAE, the tokenizer and normaliser as upstream's locked libraries build them, what reproduces upstream exactly, patch decoding with CUDA graphs, the full and LoRA fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[10937,"The waits were removed with exact equivalents of upstream's idioms (masked assignments, list indices, Python scalars stored into tensors, `.item()` checks), and the stop flag is read once per step. `dispatch.DEBUG`'s mask check is skipped while a stream captures (it reads back; the warm-up checked)."],[12108,"The warm request before the CPU rounds:"],[12092,"The warm runs of two rounds side by side, the speed-up, the time to first audio of streamed cases and the phases that changed most"],[14175,"The WAV is read as soundfile reads it (channels averaged) and resampled to 16 kHz by soxr (its HQ default)."],[10011,"The ways a model can be fine-tuned, with their stages and hyperparameters"],[13466,"The web UI (`mizuoto/webui/`) and the docs site (`site/`) use bun to install, build and test. `dev.py` looks for `bun` on `PATH`, then in the installer's default `~/.bun/bin`, and gives a clear error, not a traceback, when neither has it."],[14016,"The web UI is a Vue 3 project in `mizuoto/webui/`. Its components are Material Web (`@material/web`), its icons Lucide (`@lucide/vue`), its data layer TanStack Query (`@tanstack/vue-query`) with `openapi-fetch`, its state Pinia. The build, `mizuoto/webui/dist/`, ships in the wheel as package data and is served by the API's `SPAStaticFiles` (see HTTP API and command line). The base (`theme/`, `ui/`, motion, layers, the shell, stores, i18n, rule tests) is rvc-next's; where it comes from is in Design references and decisions."],[9158,"The web UI opens on **Speak**, where the dummy engine works right away (it speaks in tones); there is no setup screen. Choose the download source under **Settings** › **Downloads**, check torch under **Settings** › **Compute** (or with `mizuoto doctor`), then download models from **Models**, or with the button that replaces **Speak** when the chosen model is not downloaded, and follow them in **Jobs**. See First run."],[8355,"The web UI, built with bun (`mizuoto/webui/dist`)"],[9399,"The web UI, the HTTP API, the command line"],[13441,"The web UI: bun"],[8727,"The web UI's address, the port, whether it serves"],[15750,"The web UI's layout: navigation, the jobs sheet, the models in memory, the theme, and the guide to each screen."],[13169,"The weights in ONNX files are converted into torch modules by an in-tree protobuf reader (`runtime/convert/onnx.py`), the result cached under the model folder's `.mizuoto/`"],[15739,"The weights' version is read from the files. GPT-SoVITS models of the same version switch to these weights when they use the voice (marked **own weights** under **Which models can use it**); models of another version warn and clone as usual. **The voice keeps its clips too: the engine still needs a reference clip with the weights.** Weights exported by a training experiment are added to the voice for you."],[11636,"The Whisper encoder lives in the ASR engine and is not shared with CosyVoice's speech tokenizers"],[14179,"The windows' tokens are merged into text and timestamped segments by the pipeline's `_decode_asr`."],[9313,"The working memory set aside for a step follows the request: a language model's cache is sized by the text, not by the longest generation `max_new_tokens` allows. A generation that runs far longer than its text and outgrows the GPU runs that step again with more weights streamed, with the same result."],[11609,"Their licences (Fish Audio Research License, bilibili Model Use License) cover the code; a port is a derivative, and folding it into the GPL-3.0 `mizuoto` would conflict"],[8863,"Their results cannot be added to another engine's training datasets"],[14095,"Theme, seed colour, contrast, language, motion, last screen, Speak's last choices; kept in localStorage and synced to the server through `/api/v1/client-state/{key}`, so they follow the user across browsers"],[10335,"Then allow an engine's cheaper way (tiles, smaller batches; the output differs slightly)"],[8297,"Then binary messages: mono 16-bit little-endian PCM at the `start` rate, with `{\"type\": \"segment\", \"index\": n}` before each segment."],[15224,"Then click:"],[15911,"Then Mizuoto, in one install; add the gated engines when you want them:"],[8397,"Then open `http://<host address>:7869`; 